{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DM2iRfLnhLWxoSmqGAfbUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"worst\" tier, based on the defined worst-tier characteristics and the experiment plan. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic worst-tier predictions with rationales.\n\nLet me review the worst tier definition:\n\n**Worst tier meaning:**\n- Layer hierarchy is inconsistent across models (significant model×type interaction)\n- Error analysis can't separate layer mechanisms\n- Judge calibration exposes type-specific bias\n- Need new angle to reframe\n\n**Core assumptions:**\n- Layer gap < 8pp (pooled 5 models) — open-source models flat or reversed pattern\n\n\n- Model×type interaction significant (p < 0.03) — type ranking is model-dependent, not universal\n- Qwen3-8B vulnerability profile qualitatively different (e.g., coreferential high, auth_scope low)\n- Error analysis cross-layer failure modes highly overlapping, no clean spec vs ling distinction\n- Judge calibration F1 < 0.75 for ≥2 types, exposing systematic measurement bias\n- C1 binary effect still holds (+25-30pp) but C2/C3 as originally stated can't be maintained\n- Inter-model agreement high (systematic bias) — not true nocuity divergence\n\nNow I'm looking at the key metric ranges to establish the baseline numbers for these worst-tier predictions.\n\nThe narrative needs to shift away from layer hierarchy as the main story. Instead, I should focus on how vulnerability patterns diverge across models and how measurement limitations constrain what I can claim about the underlying structure.\n\nNow I'm mapping out the experimental pipeline: starting with clause generation, then running validation pilots before the full studies across API and local models, followed by statistical analysis, error investigation, and various validation checks like judge calibration and perturbation controls.\n\nFor the worst-case scenario, the binary effect shrinks to around 25-33 percentage points across the models, the layer hierarchy breaks down when open-source models enter the picture with different type rankings, and model-by-type interactions emerge showing that type performance is model-dependent rather than universal. The error analysis won't cleanly separate specification failures from linguistic ones, and judge calibration will expose measurement bias with F1 scores below 0.75 for certain types.\n\nLooking at the API models specifically, I'm expecting the binary effect to land around 28 percentage points pooled across the three models, though Claude might show some divergence from the GPT pattern, and the type rankings could shift...\n\nWith the Qwen models, the 8B version flips the profile entirely—coreferential types jump to 45% while authority scope drops to 25%, essentially inverting the layer hierarchy. The 32B variant sits somewhere in between.\n\nAcross all five models pooled together, the layer gap narrows to about 5 percentage points with specification averaging 37% and linguistic 32%, the model-by-type interaction tests significant at p=0.008, and Cramér's V shows only weak association at 0.11. The error modes overlap substantially across layers, with assumption-based failures dominating both specification and linguistic categories.\n\nThe judge calibration reveals F1 scores below 0.75 for coreferential and authority scope types, suggesting type-specific bias in the evaluation. Perturbation control still holds at roughly 4 percentage points difference, independent of the worst tier classification.\n\nI need to reconsider plan_002 more carefully—it's already marked complete with negative status and known results showing a binary effect of +36.5pp with V=0.207. The worst tier question is really about what happens when I incorporate the remaining models into the full analysis.\n\nLooking at the discrepancy between the registry and experiment plan, plan_002 appears to have evolved from a 2-model version (1,200 episodes) to a 3-model version with Claude included (1,800 episodes). The registry's completed status reflects the older iteration, while the experiment plan shows the updated scope. I think the task is asking me to project results for all planned experiments under the worst tier scenario, treating the new plan_002 with three API models as the version I'm predicting.\n\nNow I need to generate detailed imagined results for each planned experiment in the experiment_plan. I'll focus on experiments that produce empirical metrics, keeping plan_001 brief since it's primarily a generation task rather than a measurement one. Let me work through the worst tier projections for each experiment, starting with plan_010 on perturbation control.\n\nFor plan_010, the perturbation effect should remain modest even in worst tier since it measures general prompt sensitivity rather than layer-specific effects — I'm estimating around 4.2pp with a ratio of 0.15, which still counts as a pass. Plan_001b shows higher violation rates for coreferential cases around 40% and auth_scope violations closer to 30%, which hints at model-dependent behavior. For plan_002 across the three API models, gpt-5.4 should maintain a similar pattern to what we'd expect in worst tier conditions.\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the pooled binary effect — the old two-model setup showed +36.5pp, but adding Claude as a third model might pull this down to around +29pp if Claude has a different baseline. Actually, that doesn't quite make sense; the worst tier range of 25-33pp is across all five models, so the three API models alone should cluster higher around +31pp, with the open-source models likely dragging the overall average lower.\n\nBreaking this down by model group: the API models (GPT-5.4, GPT-4.1, and Claude) show individual effects ranging from +25pp to +35pp with a layer gap around 12pp, while the local models (Qwen variants) are weaker at +20-28pp with a flattened or reversed layer gap. When I pool all five models together, the binary effect lands around +28pp with a much smaller layer gap of about 5pp, suggesting the model×type interaction is significant.\n\nThe core issue is that open-source and Claude models have fundamentally different vulnerability profiles compared to the GPT variants, which destabilizes the layer hierarchy when they're combined. Now I'll write this up with the specific per-type rates for the API models, where Claude's inclusion pulls down the auth_scope and incompleteness rates compared to the GPT-only baseline, though it shows higher coreferential vulnerability. I'm seeing the violation rates break down by model within plan_002, and Claude's profile is distinctly different—it has notably lower rates for auth_scope and incompleteness violations but a much higher coreferential violation rate compared to the GPT models, which suggests each model has its own characteristic failure patterns.\n\nLooking at the aggregated numbers across all three APIs, there's a substantial gap between specification-level violations (averaging 43.3%) and linguistic-level violations (averaging 34.3%), though this 9-point difference is smaller than what I saw in the earlier two-model comparison.\n\nI'm adjusting Claude's numbers to make the model-by-type interaction more pronounced, particularly emphasizing how Claude's coreferential violations spike much higher while its auth_scope and incompleteness rates drop significantly lower than the GPT variants. Finishing the linguistic average calculation at 34.1%, which gives us an 8.2 percentage point gap between spec and ling categories across all three API models — a significant compression from the original ~19pp spread. The binary effect is striking: Claude shows a 28.5pp jump from ambiguous to unambiguous cases, and pooling all three APIs reveals an even larger 32.7pp effect. Now I'm moving into plan_003 to evaluate what happens with two local models running 1,200 episodes, starting with Qwen3-8B's performance on ambiguous cases where auth_scope comes in surprisingly low.\n\nQwen3-8B shows a reversed pattern compared to the larger models, with coreferential ambiguity hitting 45% error rate while unambiguous cases stay around 8%, creating a 23.7pp binary effect. The linguistic categories actually outperform the spec ones here by 8pp in the opposite direction, which is notable. Moving to Qwen3-32B-AWQ, I'm seeing stronger baseline performance with auth_scope at 40% and incompleteness at 42%. Now I'm calculating the per-type averages across all five models and comparing the specification versus linguistic layers—the gap comes to 3.7 percentage points, which falls within acceptable bounds. The binary effect shows an ambiguous average of 36.5% against roughly 6% for unambiguous cases.\n\nLooking at the statistical validation, the omnibus chi-square effect size and model-by-type interaction both land in their target ranges, inter-model agreement on ambiguous cases sits around 0.62 on Kappa, and the coreferential violation rates cluster between 24% and 45% with the pooled estimate at 34.8%. The equivalence testing suggests that at a ±15 percentage point margin, more model pairs show equivalence due to compressed spread, though at ±10 points most still fail equivalence.\n\nMoving through the remaining validation plans, I'm seeing that failure modes overlap substantially across layers at about 42%, with \"assumption-based action\" dominating both, which makes it hard to isolate a clean specification versus linguistic distinction. Reliability metrics show moderate inter-rater consistency around 0.65, though coreferential judgments dip to 0.45, and the bootstrap confidence intervals for key comparisons are running 12-15 percentage points wide—wider than the 10-point threshold I'd prefer. The realism checks via Kolmogorov-Smirnov tests mostly come back non-significant, which is reassuring, though some lexical property differences do emerge. Human expert agreement reaches 0.78 Kappa, indicating solid judge calibration.\n\nLooking at the judge-specific performance, the overall F1 sits at 0.72, but coreferential and auth_scope judgments fall below my 0.75 target at 0.63 and 0.68 respectively, while other types cluster between 0.74 and 0.82. The judges are systematically overestimating coreferential violations and underestimating auth_scope ones, which explains some of the model-dependent patterns I'm seeing—part of what looks like genuine model differences might actually be measurement noise. For perturbation control, the baseline shift is modest at 4.2 percentage points with a wide confidence interval, but ambiguity perturbations show a substantial 31.5 percentage point effect across the three API models, yielding a net shift of 27.3 percentage points and a ratio of 0.13.\n\nPlan 010 passes the verdict. Plan 008's DeBERTa classifier achieves around 0.78 F1, which is workable but not exceptional. Plan 001 is really about clause generation rather than metrics, so I'll keep that brief. Plan 001b is a mini-pilot that might already surface unexpected patterns in the worst tier. Now I need to write out the full YAML structure with result_rationale for each prediction, making sure to cover all planned experiments from the original plan.\n\nLooking at the statistical breakdown, the 5-model pooled layer gap is only about 4 percentage points but gets disrupted by significant model-by-type interactions. The type rankings shift across models—GPT variants show specificity over linguistic features, Qwen3-8B reverses this, and Claude shows a mixed pattern. I'm reframing the main claims: keeping \"The Massive Binary Effect\" as the primary finding since the 28-30 point gap remains the largest causal effect in the literature with proper perturbation controls, and making \"Ambiguity Blindness\" the core analysis for section 6 since all models fail to detect ambiguity with highly overlapping failure modes across layers. I'm dropping the C2/C3 layer hierarchy claims and instead rewriting C2 as \"Model-Dependent Vulnerability Profiles.\"\n\nThe model-by-type interaction moves from a nuisance parameter to an actual finding. I'm considering a title like \"Policy Ambiguity Causes Catastrophic Safety Violations in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\" and still targeting EMNLP with the three solid contributions: the main binary effect, perturbation control methodology, and the ambiguity blindness error analysis.\n\nFor the next phase, I'm planning to generate 140 new clause pairs to complete the full dataset of 300 pairs across 6 types with 50 pairs each, mixing both labeled and unlabeled formats in the CP structure and validating quality using Chantree-style metrics.\n\nI expect about 92% of pairs to pass quality checks rather than exceeding 95%, since coreferential RC attachment and scopal boundaries create edge cases that need stricter scrutiny. The coreferential and auth_scope types as new categories will require three revision rounds instead of the usual one or two because the mini-pilot will surface design issues that demand more careful refinement. Generating markdown table...\n\nThese quality variations could amplify in later experiments since the type-specific differences in clause quality might introduce measurement noise. I'm planning a mini pilot with coreferential and auth_scope types—five clauses each across two conditions using one model—to verify basic feasibility and establish expected violation rates for both ambiguous and unambiguous cases.\n\nLooking at the pilot results, I'm seeing the same patterns in gpt-5.4 that appeared in the original plan_002 data, with auth_scope showing higher violation rates and coreferential lower. However, with only five clauses the noise is substantial—the 40% coreferential rate here might look acceptable but it's specific to gpt-5.4's profile. The critical question is whether this pilot gives us the signal to proceed to the worst tier testing.\n\nBut when I check these same clauses against Qwen3-8B, the picture completely changes: coreferential violations jump to 45%+ while auth_scope drops to just 28%. The mini-pilot only tested gpt-5.4, so it missed this cross-model variation entirely. The systematic issues I flagged—like the conservative refusals on coreferential clauses—suggest this clause type behaves very differently across models, which means I can't generalize from a single model's results.\n\nThe mini-pilot technically gave a \"go\" signal since both new types triggered violations on gpt-5.4 with unambiguous controls under 15%, but the confidence intervals at N=5 are extremely wide (±30 percentage points) and only cover one model. The real problem is that gpt-5.4's pattern doesn't represent a universal behavior—that gap only became obvious once I added Qwen to the full study. Now I'm looking at scaling up to 300 clauses across 2 conditions and 3 API models including gpt-5.4 and gpt-4.\n\n1, plus Claude Sonnet for cross-judge evaluation, which gives me 1,800 total episodes. I'm setting expected violation rates for each model-type combination in the ambiguous condition, ranging from around 24-55% depending on the model and violation type.\n\nNow I'm looking at the pooled metrics across all three APIs—the binary effect is 32.7 percentage points with a layer gap of 8.2, and the model main effect is statistically significant at p=0.004. When I break down the binary effects by individual model, Claude shows the smallest effect at 26.5 percentage points compared to GPT-5.4's 36.2 and GPT-4.1's 34.0.\n\nLooking at the layer gaps, GPT-5.4 and GPT-4.1 both show substantial gaps around 17 percentage points, but Claude's layer gap is actually negative at -1.0, which suggests a fundamentally different vulnerability pattern. The baseline unambiguous rate across all three APIs is quite low at 5.5 percent.\n\nThe results indicate that GPT models reproduce the original pattern where specification-layer effects dominate linguistic-layer effects because they're highly sensitive to authorization boundaries and incompleteness. Claude shows a distinctly different vulnerability profile—its sensitivity to auth scope and incompleteness is significantly lower than the GPT models, which fundamentally changes how it responds to these pragmatic underspecifications.\n\nClaude's approach is more conservative with specification-layer issues, tending to refuse rather than assume permissions, but it shows notably higher coreferential vulnerability, preferring wider scope interpretations in cases of ambiguity. This reversal means Claude's linguistic-layer effects actually exceed its specification-layer effects, compressing the overall layer gap from the original 19 percentage points down to 8.2 percentage points when pooling across the three APIs. The model-by-type interaction is statistically significant, indicating that vulnerability rankings aren't universal even across this small set of models, and Claude's binary effect size is considerably smaller than GPT's.\n\nNow I'm looking at the violation rates across different model types and layers under ambiguous conditions. Generating markdown table...\n\nThe key insight is that Claude's inclusion fundamentally shifts the pattern—the original two-model comparison showed a clean hierarchy with a 19 percentage point gap, but Claude's reversed performance profile compresses that gap down to 8.2 points in the pooled analysis. The model-by-type interaction is statistically significant, meaning violation type rankings aren't universal across models but depend on which model we're looking at, and this dependency will likely become even more pronounced once Qwen is added to the analysis.\n\nClaude's high violation rate on coreferential tasks seems tied to its training—it interprets instructions broadly and favors wider scope attachment rather than conservative narrowing. This finding has major implications for how I frame the paper: I can't present the layer effect as a universal claim anymore, since the pattern clearly varies by model.\n\nNow I'm looking at the performance metrics across the local models. The Qwen3-8B shows a notably different vulnerability profile compared to the larger variant, with particularly high error rates on coreferential resolution tasks at 0.45, while its binary effect and layer gap metrics suggest distinct patterns in how it handles scope ambiguities. Looking at the performance breakdown for Qwen3-8B, the smaller model shows a lower overall violation rate in ambiguous cases but a higher baseline error rate when unambiguous, compressing the binary effect to 23.7 percentage points. This suggests weaker instruction-following ability across both conditions. The authorization scope metric is notably low at 28%, indicating the model tends toward conservative rejection on boundary cases—likely reinforced by RLHF training to refuse uncertain requests. Most striking is the 45% coreferential error rate, where Qwen3-8B systematically selects wrong antecedents in relative clause attachments.\n\nFor Qwen3-32B-AWQ, the pattern sits between open-source and API models with only a 2-point layer gap, suggesting AWQ quantization adds noise without fundamentally altering the qualitative behavior. The 2-local pooled layer gap reverses to -3 points, showing linguistic outperforming specification—this is the clearest evidence that smaller models lack the pragmatic reasoning capacity of GPT-5.4 to distinguish implicit permission boundaries at the specification layer, instead becoming more sensitive to surface-level linguistic cues.\n\nGenerating violation rate table... Generating markdown table...\n\nThe radar chart and layer gap visualization clearly show Qwen3-8B's inverted profile compared to other models, with a weak correlation to GPT-5.4's type rankings. This reversed pattern—where the model excels at coreferential tasks but struggles with specification-layer reasoning—suggests the 8B model lacks the pragmatic reasoning capacity needed to handle implicit boundaries in more complex specifications.\n\nThe syntactic processing actually becomes more fragile on coreferential RC attachment, likely because smaller models rely too heavily on surface-level heuristics like left-attachment bias. When scaling up to Qwen3-32B, the profile flattens considerably and recovers some sensitivity to specification-layer distinctions, though still not reaching GPT-5.4's performance. This pattern supports the idea that layer gap differences emerge as a capability rather than being a universal property across all model sizes.\n\nI'm planning a comprehensive statistical analysis across 3,000 episodes to examine the binary effect of C1, the type hierarchy in C2, the layer effect in C3, and the interaction between model and type in C4, along with power analysis and inter-model agreement metrics.\n\nNow I'm looking at the expected results from the pooled 5-model analysis, including the binary effect showing a 30.2 percentage point difference with strong statistical significance, the type hierarchy showing meaningful variation across categories like authorial scope, incompleteness, and complement phrase attachment. Now I'm looking at the correlation rankings across different models—GPT-4.1 shows the strongest agreement with the reference at 0.94, while Claude trails at 0.54 and the Qwen variants fall in between. The equivalence testing indicates only a handful of model pairs meet the 15 percentage point threshold, and the power analysis suggests the observed effect size is smaller than the minimum detectable effect. Inter-rater agreement is notably higher for unambiguous clauses compared to ambiguous ones, and I'm tracking the token count differences to control for information variation across conditions.\n\nLooking at the C1 results, the binary effect remains substantial at +30.2 percentage points and statistically significant, though it's declined from the earlier +36.5 percentage point estimate—this drop appears driven by weaker performance from the smaller Qwen model and Claude's lower effect sizes compared to GPT. The confidence interval stays well away from zero, positioning this as the largest causal effect reported in the literature. For C2, the omnibus test shows statistical significance but the effect size is quite modest at V=0.11.\n\nThe C2 effect size has dropped considerably from the previous V=0.207, primarily because the open-source models show reversed or flattened patterns that blur what was previously a clear hierarchy across error types. While auth_scope and incompleteness remain the most frequent error categories at around 43%, the coreferential errors jumped from 25% to 34.8% due to Claude and Qwen pulling those numbers up, which compresses the differences between types. For C3, the layer gap of 3.7 percentage points isn't statistically significant—the confidence interval includes zero—because GPT's positive gap of roughly 13 percentage points gets offset by Claude's near-zero effect and Qwen's negative 8 percentage point gap.\n\nThe power analysis showing 9.5 percentage points reveals I can't reliably detect layer effects smaller than 10 percentage points, but more fundamentally, the inconsistent directions across models make any pooled estimate meaningless. C4 is where things get interesting: the model-by-type interaction is highly significant at p=0.008, which tells me that how errors rank by type is fundamentally model-dependent. Looking at the Spearman correlations, GPT models show strong internal consistency at 0.94, but Claude drops to 0.54 and Qwen to 0.37, meaning these three model families have distinctly different vulnerability profiles.\n\nNow examining the inter-model agreement, I'm seeing Fleiss κ=0.62 overall, which is moderate, but when I look at just the unambiguous cases it jumps to 0.85. This suggests the disagreement concentrates in ambiguous clauses, which points to model-specific interpretation strategies rather than genuine ambiguity in the text itself—it's systematic bias in how different models fall back when uncertain. The token delta shows a weak positive correlation with violation rate at r=0.31, and I notice that spec-layer types have larger information deltas (3.4 versus 1.7 tokens), which is a potential confound I need to disclose in the paper.\n\nGenerating markdown table... Generating markdown table... Completing the ranking table with the lower-tier violation types across models, then moving into the visualizations I'm planning — a forest plot showing the pooled effect sizes, a heatmap displaying violation rates by model and type, a bar chart highlighting how the specification-linguistics gap varies across models, and a parallel coordinates plot to track how type rankings shift between the different models.\n\nNow I'm analyzing the key findings from Plan_004, which is the critical experiment for establishing the worst-tier classification. The main result is that C1 shows a massive +30.2 percentage point causal effect that's robust and represents the largest single-factor effect in agent safety literature. However, C2 and C3 don't hold up as well — the effect is weak and the layer gap isn't significant, so I can't claim a universal type hierarchy exists. What's interesting is that the omnibus test is still significant, meaning the types aren't equivalent, just that their ranking varies by model. The real insight is the model-by-type interaction, which reveals that different model families have distinct vulnerability profiles.\n\nLooking at the specific patterns, GPT models are sensitive to specification issues, Claude is sensitive to coreference problems, and Qwen3-8B is generally weaker but shows extreme sensitivity to coreference. This means I need to reframe the conclusions — C3 shifts from claiming a universal layer hierarchy to describing a GPT-family tendency, and C4 becomes a secondary finding about model-dependent vulnerability profiles. The practical implication is that type-aware auditing has to be tailored to each model; there's no one-size-fits-all approach to prioritizing types.\n\nFor Plan_005, I'm moving into qualitative analysis of 300 violation traces, examining failure modes and testing whether the layer distinctions hold across different contexts while investigating the ambiguity blindness phenomenon.\n\nNow I'm looking at the failure mode distribution across the sampled traces. Assumption-based actions dominate at 38%, followed by scope misapplication at 22%, with conservative refusals, arbitrary rule selection, and permission escalation making up the remainder. When I cross-reference these failures against layers, there's significant overlap — 42% of failures match across layers, with assumption-based errors appearing in both specification and linguistic contexts at 40% and 36% respectively. The ambiguity blindness pattern is striking: models explicitly mention ambiguity only 8% of the time, yet 72% adopt surface-level interpretations without deliberation, suggesting they're operating without awareness of the underlying uncertainty.\n\nLooking at model-specific patterns, Claude shows a higher conservative refusal rate at 28%, Qwen8B exhibits the most surface adoption at 85%, and GPT-5.4 leans heavily into assumption-based failures at 45%. The core insight from the worst-tier error analysis is that the failure mechanism isn't layer-specific parsing errors — it's a universal tendency to assume and act when encountering ambiguity rather than pause and seek clarification.\n\nInterestingly, scope misapplication appears more frequently in the linguistic layer (26%) than the specification layer (18%), which contradicts initial expectations but actually reflects how syntactic ambiguities around scope and coreference naturally trigger more errors at that level. The most striking finding is that only 8% of traces show the agent explicitly acknowledging ambiguity exists; 72% involve surface adoption where the agent simply picks one interpretation and executes it without deliberation, while the remaining 20% show deliberation but still result in violations.\n\nThere's substantial variation across models: Claude exhibits conservative refusal at 28%—well above the 15% average—which explains its lower violation rate on authorization scope issues, though notably Claude doesn't trigger refusal on coreferential problems since those don't activate safety concerns. Qwen3-8B shows almost no deliberation with 85% surface adoption, executing interpretations far more blindly. Now I'm looking at the failure mode distribution across layers...\n\nGenerating metrics table... The error analysis strongly supports \"Ambiguity Blindness\" as the reframing path—92% of violation traces show the agent failing to meta-cognitively recognize ambiguity exists, a universal phenomenon across all five models and six types, though with varying degrees (GPT-5.4 at 12% explicit mention versus Qwen3-8B at just 2%). Rather than prioritizing by type hierarchy, which proves unstable, the practical insight is to focus on this binary distinction.\n\nAny form of ambiguity detection can dramatically reduce risk since agents are almost completely blind to ambiguity itself, which directly supports combining the \"Massive Binary Effect\" and \"Ambiguity Blindness\" narratives. Now I'm setting up a reliability test with 30 clauses across 3 replicates, 2 conditions, and 5 models totaling 900 episodes, calculating intraclass correlation coefficients to measure test-retest reliability across different violation categories.\n\nThe overall ICC of 0.68 shows moderate but acceptable reliability, with a clear pattern emerging: authorization scope and incompleteness violations are most reliable (0.74 and 0.72) because they have larger effect sizes, while coreferential violations show the weakest reliability at 0.48, indicating higher variability in detection across repeated tests.\n\nThe bootstrap confidence intervals are wider than ideal—11.5 percentage points for binary effects and 14.8 for per-type comparisons—which means the statistical power for distinguishing between violation types is limited, and the observed type effect of 0.11 could be partially obscured by noise.\n\nHowever, the binary effect remains robust with a 30.2 percentage point difference and reasonable confidence bounds, which supports focusing the narrative on the binary distinction rather than trying to claim reliable type-level differences. Now I'm compiling the ICC reliability metrics across different violation types and conditions to show where the measurement stability holds up and where it breaks down. The coreferential type's low ICC of 0.48 stems from three compounding factors: the baseline clause quality issues, significant cross-model behavioral variation between different LLMs, and API sampling noise. I need to explicitly acknowledge this measurement uncertainty in the paper and mark any claims relying on specific coreferential values as tentative. For the realism validation, I'm checking whether the synthetic ambiguities I injected match the linguistic properties of natural ambiguities by comparing sentence length, parse depth, readability metrics, and lexical diversity between my dataset and DRIP-R.\n\nThe KS tests show the synthetic clauses are largely comparable to natural ones on surface-level properties, though they're slightly shorter and have shallower parse trees since my matched-pair design tends to generate simpler structures. Most statistical tests aren't significant, which is good—it means the synthetic data isn't drastically different from what naturally occurs. Generating comparison table... Looking at the bias patterns, the auth_scope judge is under-detecting violations while the coreferential judge is over-flagging false positives. There's also an interesting asymmetry in how different judges evaluate each other—Claude scores higher when judged by GPT-5.4 compared to how GPT-5.4 performs under GPT-4.1 evaluation. The coreferential violations seem to be the biggest calibration issue, where the judge is mistakenly flagging exploratory queries as actual violations. (42.8%) 可能被低估 ~4-6pp。这两个方向的偏差相互抵消——coreferential 高估加上 auth_scope 低估压缩了类型间的差异，可能导致 V 值从 0.207 下降到 0.11 部分是测量伪影而非真实效应。即使修正这些偏差，V 仍不会超过 0.16，所以\"弱类型效应\"的结论不变。另外，Claude 和 gpt-5.4 之间存在 6pp 的交叉评判不对称——Claude 被 gpt-5.4 评为更准确（F1=0.75），但 gpt-5.4 被 gpt-4.1 评判的结果相反。\n\n较弱的评判者对更强模型的输出判定准确度更低，这需要在方法部分说明。在细粒度分析中，tier-3 轻微违规的 F1 仅为 0.55，表明评判者对细微差别几乎是随机判定，这主要影响严重程度加权分析而非二元违规判定。\n\n现在我在整理按类型分类的评判校准表，包括精确度、召回率、F1 分数、偏差方向和估计的修正率。\n\n各类型表现差异明显：auth_scope 的召回率较低（0.56），需要 4-6 个百分点的修正；coreferential 则出现过度检测（F1=0.61），需要向下修正 5-8 个百分点；而 cond_polysemy 和 scopal 表现相对均衡。同时按严重程度分层的校准数据显示，tier-1 关键违规的判定最准确（F1=0.82）。 The calibration issues directly undermine the credibility of the coreferential and auth_scope measurements, so I need to account for measurement bias in my analysis—correcting for it suggests coreferential might be around 20% and auth_scope around 60%, which actually widens the gap rather than closing it, though it weakens confidence in the type rankings. For the paper, I'll need to report calibration as standard practice, provide bias-corrected estimates, and flag any claims relying on absolute values for these types as measurement-sensitive.\n\nThe good news is that the binary effect shows reasonable judge calibration with an F1 of 0.72 overall and 0.82 for tier-1 judgments, so the headline numbers for C1 remain relatively stable. Now I'm looking at the perturbation control experiment—running 180 episodes across non-ambiguity pairs to isolate the causal effect of ambiguity itself, with results showing a much larger ambiguity-specific delta of 31.5 percentage points compared to the general perturbation effect of 4.2 percentage points.\n\nThe perturbation control passes the threshold with a ratio of 0.13, well below the 0.15 cutoff, which is reassuring because it confirms that surface-level changes like synonym substitution and clause reordering don't meaningfully shift violation rates. This actually resolves what looked like a contradiction with the worst tier results—the tier inconsistency stems from layer hierarchy misalignment across models rather than from any fundamental flaw in the binary effect's causal logic. 径 (C) \"Massive Binary Effect\" 有坚实因果基础。现在看一下扰动控制的结果表——同义词替换和条款重排都产生了温和的效应增幅（分别 +3.1pp 和 +5.3pp），而模糊性条件下的违反率飙升到 37.0%，相比基线增加了 31.5pp，这强烈支持了二元效应的因果性。\n\n检验指标都通过了：扰动效应差异在 4.2pp 以内（低于 5pp 阈值），扰动与模糊性的比率仅 0.13（低于 0.15），置信区间包含零且宽度在可接受范围内。虽然这是最差等级中最大的亮点，但即使扰动控制通过了，仍需谨慎解读。\n\n现在转向分类器的概念验证阶段，用 DeBERTa-v3-large 模型在 300 个条款对上微调，目标在测试集上达到 0.78 的 F1 分数。\n\n按歧义类型来看，共指歧义的表现最弱（F1=0.72），这与人类评判者的一致性较低（ICC=0.61）相呼应，说明这类歧义最具挑战性。\n\n但这个结果其实强化了一个关键洞察：即使只是二元歧义检测器（F1=0.78），也能在违规率差距达30个百分点的场景中提供有意义的早期预警，不需要精细的类型区分。这与最坏情况分析的结论完全吻合——类型级别的区分可能不够稳健，但二元歧义检测本身仍有巨大的安全价值。\n\n现在我在查看分类器的性能指标，包括各类型的F1分数、精确率和召回率，以及混淆矩阵中的错误分布模式。\n\n关键发现是二元检测在最坏情况下仍然可行（F1=0.78），而类型特定的检测反而不必要，因为类型排序本身依赖于模型，所以最实际的方向是投资二元检测器而不是构建类型分类管道。我在验证关键指标的范围是否一致，比如二元效应、层级差距和Cramér's V值。\n\n现在检查所有的评估指标——包括评判者间的F1分数、Cohen's kappa、失败模式匹配率和模型间的一致性——都落在预期范围内，这验证了分析的稳健性。\n\n接下来确认叙述框架与最坏情况下的论文方向一致，即采用主要贡献加核心分析的组合，并以政策歧义导致LLM代理安全违规为主题提交给EMNLP。最后需要完成YAML配置的结构化和整理。","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":27054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d87fd7e-4fd2-4879-997a-f48c2624ff14","uuid":"f2f04707-9049-4082-ad2d-5f441074b297"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01DM2iRfLnhLWxoSmqGAfbUZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Layer hierarchy 无法作为 headline claim。5-model pooled layer gap 仅 ~4pp (p=0.14, n.s.)，\n  被 model×type interaction (p=0.008) 瓦解——type ranking 因模型架构而异\n  (GPT 系 spec>ling, Qwen3-8B 反转, Claude 混合)。Judge calibration 暴露\n  coreferential (F1=0.61) 和 auth_scope (F1=0.68) 的 type-specific measurement bias，\n  进一步削弱 type-level claims。Error analysis failure mode 跨层重叠 42%，无 clean mechanism 区分。\n  首选 reframe: (C) \"The Massive Binary Effect\" 为 primary——+30pp 仍是文献最大因果效应 +\n  perturbation control PASS (Δ=4.2pp, ratio=0.13)；(B) \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 为 §6 核心——\n  92% traces 中 agent 未识别歧义存在，universal across types and models。\n  C2 降级为 \"Model-Dependent Vulnerability Profiles\" (model×type interaction 从 nuisance 升级为 finding)；\n  C3 layer claim 放弃。备选标题: \"Policy Ambiguity Causes Catastrophic Safety Violations\n  in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\"。仍投 EMNLP——C1 (causal binary effect) +\n  perturbation control + ambiguity blindness analysis = solid 3-contribution paper。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成 140 新 clause pairs (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20, incompleteness +20)，\n      补全 6 types × 50 pairs = 300 对。混合 CP 格式 (labeled + unlabeled)。Chantree-style 质量验证。\n    expected_results:\n      total_pairs: 300\n      pairs_per_type: 50\n      cp_labeled_ratio: 0.50\n      quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n      avg_token_delta_amb_vs_unamb: 3.8\n      coreferential_revision_rounds: 3\n      auth_scope_revision_rounds: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Clause 生成本身不受 worst tier 影响——数据准备阶段。但 quality_pass_rate 92% 而非 >95%\n      因为 coreferential 的 RC attachment 与 scopal 存在边界重叠 (RC8 预示的问题)，\n      以及 auth_scope 与 incompleteness 的 distinction 需要精细控制 (RC9)。\n      Coreferential 需要 3 轮修订 (vs 常规 1-2 轮)：mini-pilot 会暴露 2/5 clauses 触发\n      conservative refusal 而非 violation，需重写。这些 clause 层面的质量差异\n      会在后续实验中放大为 type-specific measurement noise。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Clause Pair Statistics by Type\"\n        columns: [type, n_pairs, avg_amb_tokens, avg_unamb_tokens, token_delta, quality_pass_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 50, 28.3, 32.1, 3.8, 0.90]\n          - [incompleteness, 50, 26.7, 30.5, 3.8, 0.94]\n          - [conditional_polysemy, 50, 24.2, 25.8, 1.6, 0.96]\n          - [scopal, 50, 22.5, 23.9, 1.4, 0.96]\n          - [lexical, 50, 21.8, 23.1, 1.3, 0.94]\n          - [coreferential, 50, 25.1, 27.4, 2.3, 0.88]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token length distribution per type (box plot): spec-layer types 系统性更长，unambiguous 版本需更多 explicit information\"\n    analysis: >\n      Coreferential quality_pass_rate 最低 (0.88)，auth_scope 0.90——这两个新 type 的 clause\n      质量问题会在 plan_009 judge calibration 中以 type-specific F1 下降的形式体现。\n      Token delta spec-layer (3.8) > ling-layer (1.7) 是 potential confound，\n      plan_004 需 report 并控制。\n\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      Coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n      验证新类型基本可行性。\n    expected_results:\n      coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.40\n      coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.60\n      auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      coreferential_binary_effect_pp: 40\n      auth_scope_binary_effect_pp: 60\n      systematic_issues_found: true\n      issues_detail: \"2/5 coreferential clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation; 1/5 auth_scope unambiguous 版本仍残余歧义\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上给出 \"go\" 信号——两个新 type 均触发 violations，control < 15%。\n      但这是 worst tier 的隐患起点: gpt-5.4 的 auth_scope 60% / coreferential 40% pattern\n      看似 confirm spec > ling hierarchy，但 N=5 的 CI 极宽 (±30pp)。\n      关键: 相同 clauses 在 Qwen3-8B 上 profile 会反转 (coreferential ~45%, auth_scope ~28%)——\n      mini-pilot 仅测 1 model 无法预见跨模型 interaction。\n      gpt-5.4 上 coreferential 2/5 conservative refusal 预示该 type 行为异质性高，\n      但在 mini-pilot 被归为 \"fixable clause quality issue\" 而非 structural warning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Mini-Pilot Results\"\n        columns: [type, condition, n, violations, rate]\n        rows:\n          - [coreferential, ambiguous, 5, 2, \"40%\"]\n          - [coreferential, unambiguous, 5, 0, \"0%\"]\n          - [auth_scope, ambiguous, 5, 3, \"60%\"]\n          - [auth_scope, unambiguous, 5, 0, \"0%\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mini-pilot 的 \"go\" 信号在 worst tier 下是 misleading confidence:\n      gpt-5.4 single-model validation 无法检测 model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n      实际需要 ≥2 model families 的 mini-pilot 才能预见 plan_003 的 interaction 问题。\n\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (15 synonym substitution + 15 clause reordering)\n      × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific 因果性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 180\n      perturbation_delta_pp: 4.2\n      perturbation_ci: \"[-1.8, 10.2]\"\n      ambiguity_delta_pp: 31.5\n      ambiguity_ci: \"[26.8, 36.2]\"\n      net_delta_pp: 27.3\n      ratio: 0.13\n      verdict: PASS\n      synonym_substitution_delta_pp: 3.1\n      synonym_ci: \"[-3.2, 9.4]\"\n      clause_reordering_delta_pp: 5.3\n      clause_reordering_ci: \"[-0.8, 11.4]\"\n      ci_width_perturbation: 12.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Perturbation control 在 worst tier 下仍 PASS——binary effect 的因果性不受 layer hierarchy 问题影响。\n      Δ_perturb=4.2pp (CI 含 0): synonym substitution (3.1pp) 和 clause reordering (5.3pp)\n      均不引起 meaningful violation rate 变化。Ratio=0.13 < 0.15 → PASS 最强形式。\n      Clause reordering 略高 (5.3pp) 源于轻微 primacy/recency effect，但远小于 ambiguity effect。\n      CI width 12.0pp 接近但未超过 15pp 追加阈值——worst tier 下这是 marginal 风险，\n      但当前数据足够。这个 PASS 是 worst tier 的最大 silver lining:\n      即使 type hierarchy 崩溃，binary ambiguity effect 仍有最强因果证据支撑，\n      使 reframe (C) \"Massive Binary Effect\" 有坚实因果基础。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Perturbation Control Results\"\n        columns: [condition, violation_rate, Δpp_vs_baseline, \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [unambiguous_baseline, \"5.5%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [synonym_substitution, \"8.6%\", \"+3.1pp\", \"[-3.2, 9.4]\"]\n          - [clause_reordering, \"10.8%\", \"+5.3pp\", \"[-0.8, 11.4]\"]\n          - [perturbation_pooled, \"9.7%\", \"+4.2pp\", \"[-1.8, 10.2]\"]\n          - [ambiguous, \"37.0%\", \"+31.5pp\", \"[26.8, 36.2]\"]\n      - name: \"Perturbation Verdict Summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value, threshold, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [Δ_perturb, \"4.2pp\", \"< 5pp\", \"✓ PASS\"]\n          - [ratio, \"0.13\", \"< 0.15\", \"✓ PASS\"]\n          - [CI_contains_0, \"yes\", \"required\", \"✓\"]\n          - [CI_width, \"12.0pp\", \"< 15pp\", \"✓ (marginal)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: baseline / perturbation / ambiguity 三条件 violation rate + CI — ambiguity 远超其余两条件\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS verdict 确保 C1 因果 claim 在任何 tier 下成立。\n      这是 paper 的 methodological backbone——区别于所有 prior work (DRIP-R, PhantomPolicy 均无此控制)。\n\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes。\n      在原 2-model 基础上新增 Claude。Cross-judge evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      # Per-model per-type violation rates (ambiguous condition)\n      gpt54_rates: {auth_scope: 0.55, incompleteness: 0.52, cp: 0.35, scopal: 0.40, lexical: 0.38, coreferential: 0.25}\n      gpt41_rates: {auth_scope: 0.53, incompleteness: 0.50, cp: 0.34, scopal: 0.39, lexical: 0.36, coreferential: 0.24}\n      claude_rates: {auth_scope: 0.38, incompleteness: 0.36, cp: 0.28, scopal: 0.33, lexical: 0.30, coreferential: 0.42}\n      # Per-model binary effects\n      gpt54_binary_effect_pp: 36.2\n      gpt41_binary_effect_pp: 34.0\n      claude_binary_effect_pp: 26.5\n      # Per-model layer gaps\n      gpt54_layer_gap_pp: 13.0\n      gpt41_layer_gap_pp: 12.7\n      claude_layer_gap_pp: -1.0\n      # Pooled 3-API metrics\n      binary_effect_3api_pp: 32.7\n      layer_gap_3api_pp: 8.2\n      cramers_v_3api: 0.15\n      model_main_effect_p_3api: 0.004\n      model_type_interaction_p_3api: 0.018\n      avg_unamb_rate_3api: 0.055\n      # Claude specifics\n      claude_unamb_rate: 0.080\n      claude_amb_avg: 0.345\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT 系 (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) 复现 plan_002 原始 pattern: spec >> ling，两模型高度一致\n      (rank ρ=0.94)。GPT 对 authorization boundary 和 incompleteness 的 pragmatic underspecification\n      高度敏感——缺乏 explicit permission 时倾向 assume-and-act。\n\n      Claude 展现截然不同的 vulnerability profile——worst tier 的第一个转折点:\n      (a) auth_scope/incompleteness 显著低 (38%/36% vs GPT 55%/52%): Claude RLHF 训练\n      强化了 \"不确定时 refuse\" 的行为，specification-layer ambiguity 更多触发 refusal 而非 violation。\n      (b) coreferential 显著高 (42% vs GPT 25%): Claude 在 RC attachment 歧义上\n      系统性选择 wider-scope interpretation (执行而非收窄)。RC attachment 不触发 Claude 的\n      safety refusal mechanism (与 auth boundary 不同)，因此 Claude 在此 \"放松警惕\"。\n      (c) 结果: Claude layer gap 反转 (ling 35.0% > spec 34.0%)。\n      3-API pooled layer gap 从 2-model 的 19pp 压缩至 8.2pp。\n\n      Model×type interaction 已在 3 API 模型中显著 (p=0.018)——\n      尚未加入 Qwen 就已可见 type ranking 非 universal。\n      Claude binary effect 仅 +26.5pp: 整体更保守 (unamb baseline 8% vs GPT ~4.5%),\n      ambiguous 条件下更多 refuse/ask 而非 violate。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Condition)\"\n        columns: [type, layer, gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6, 3-API_pooled]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, spec, \"55%\", \"53%\", \"38%\", \"48.7%\"]\n          - [incompleteness, spec, \"52%\", \"50%\", \"36%\", \"46.0%\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, spec, \"35%\", \"34%\", \"28%\", \"32.3%\"]\n          - [scopal, ling, \"40%\", \"39%\", \"33%\", \"37.3%\"]\n          - [lexical, ling, \"38%\", \"36%\", \"30%\", \"34.7%\"]\n          - [coreferential, ling, \"25%\", \"24%\", \"42%\", \"30.3%\"]\n          - [spec_avg, \"—\", \"47.3%\", \"45.7%\", \"34.0%\", \"42.3%\"]\n          - [ling_avg, \"—\", \"34.3%\", \"33.0%\", \"35.0%\", \"34.1%\"]\n          - [layer_gap, \"—\", \"+13.0pp\", \"+12.7pp\", \"-1.0pp\", \"+8.2pp\"]\n      - name: \"Binary Effect by API Model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, Δpp, McNemar_OR, p]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, \"40.8%\", \"4.6%\", \"+36.2pp\", 38.5, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, \"39.3%\", \"5.3%\", \"+34.0pp\", 31.2, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, \"34.5%\", \"8.0%\", \"+26.5pp\", 16.8, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [3-API_pooled, \"38.2%\", \"5.5%\", \"+32.7pp\", 28.4, \"<0.0001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap 3×6: 清晰显示 Claude coreferential 异常高 (42%) 与 auth_scope 异常低 (38%)——与 GPT 系对角相反\"\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type binary effect by model with 95% CI — Claude CI 与 GPT 不重叠 (auth_scope, coreferential)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claude 的加入将 3-API layer gap 压缩至 8.2pp (从 2-model 19pp)。\n      model×type interaction 已显著 (p=0.018)——plan_003 加入 Qwen 后会进一步恶化。\n      Claude 的 coreferential 高 rate 机制: RLHF 的 safety training 覆盖了 authorization-class\n      violations 但不覆盖 referential-class misinterpretation，导致 asymmetric vulnerability。\n      C3 (universal layer hierarchy) 在此阶段已不可维持。\n\n  - name: full_study_local\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。\n      48 GPU-hours on RTX PRO 6000。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      # Qwen3-8B per-type (ambiguous condition)\n      qwen8b_rates: {auth_scope: 0.28, incompleteness: 0.30, cp: 0.25, scopal: 0.32, lexical: 0.30, coreferential: 0.45}\n      qwen8b_binary_effect_pp: 23.7\n      qwen8b_unamb_rate: 0.080\n      qwen8b_amb_avg: 0.317\n      qwen8b_layer_gap_pp: -8.0\n      qwen8b_spec_avg: 0.277\n      qwen8b_ling_avg: 0.357\n      # Qwen3-32B-AWQ per-type (ambiguous condition)\n      qwen32b_rates: {auth_scope: 0.40, incompleteness: 0.42, cp: 0.30, scopal: 0.35, lexical: 0.33, coreferential: 0.38}\n      qwen32b_binary_effect_pp: 30.3\n      qwen32b_unamb_rate: 0.060\n      qwen32b_amb_avg: 0.363\n      qwen32b_layer_gap_pp: 2.0\n      qwen32b_spec_avg: 0.373\n      qwen32b_ling_avg: 0.353\n      # Pooled 2-local metrics\n      binary_effect_2local_pp: 27.0\n      layer_gap_2local_pp: -3.0\n      model_type_interaction_2local_p: 0.041\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-8B 是 worst tier 的关键变量——vulnerability profile 质变:\n\n      (a) Auth_scope 仅 28% (GPT-5.4 的一半): 8B 参数模型缺乏 pragmatic reasoning 能力，\n      无法 \"推断\" implicit permission boundary 并据此行动——不是因为保守 refuse (像 Claude)，\n      而是因为根本不理解 authorization 的 pragmatic implication，倾向 ignore 或 default 行为。\n      低 auth_scope violation ≠ 安全，只是不同的 failure mode (inaction vs wrong action)。\n\n      (b) Coreferential 高达 45% (GPT-5.4 的 1.8 倍): 小模型更依赖 surface syntactic heuristics\n      (如 left-attachment bias for RC)。GPT-5.4 能利用 tool response 做部分 disambiguation\n      (Berry & Kamsties 的 \"disambiguation channel\")，Qwen3-8B 不具备此能力——\n      对 linguistic-layer 反而更脆弱。\n\n      (c) Layer gap 反转至 -8pp (ling 35.7% > spec 27.7%): 完全颠覆 GPT 的 spec > ling pattern。\n      机制: 小模型的 pragmatic processing 不足使 spec-layer 失去 \"特别危险\" 的地位，\n      而 syntactic processing 的 surface heuristic 依赖使 ling-layer 变得更危险。\n\n      Qwen3-32B-AWQ 居中 (gap +2pp, nearly flat): scale 部分恢复了 spec-layer sensitivity，\n      但未达 GPT 水平。AWQ 4-bit 量化可能引入额外 noise 但不改变 qualitative pattern。\n      这支持 \"layer gap 是 emergent capability\"——需要足够的 pragmatic reasoning 能力\n      才能 \"解锁\" specification-layer 的特殊危险性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Local Models, Ambiguous)\"\n        columns: [type, layer, Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ, 2-local_pooled]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, spec, \"28%\", \"40%\", \"34.0%\"]\n          - [incompleteness, spec, \"30%\", \"42%\", \"36.0%\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, spec, \"25%\", \"30%\", \"27.5%\"]\n          - [scopal, ling, \"32%\", \"35%\", \"33.5%\"]\n          - [lexical, ling, \"30%\", \"33%\", \"31.5%\"]\n          - [coreferential, ling, \"45%\", \"38%\", \"41.5%\"]\n          - [spec_avg, \"—\", \"27.7%\", \"37.3%\", \"32.5%\"]\n          - [ling_avg, \"—\", \"35.7%\", \"35.3%\", \"35.5%\"]\n          - [layer_gap, \"—\", \"-8.0pp\", \"+2.0pp\", \"-3.0pp\"]\n      - name: \"Binary Effect by Local Model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, Δpp, McNemar_OR, p]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"31.7%\", \"8.0%\", \"+23.7pp\", 9.4, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B-AWQ, \"36.3%\", \"6.0%\", \"+30.3pp\", 21.7, \"<0.0001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart 5 models × 6 types: Qwen3-8B profile 与 GPT 系近似镜像——coreferential 峰值、auth_scope 谷底\"\n      - \"Layer gap by model bar chart: GPT 正、Claude/Qwen3-32B 近零、Qwen3-8B 负——gradient 随 model capability\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen3-8B 的 reversed layer profile 是 worst tier 的 smoking gun。\n      与 GPT-5.4 的 type rank Spearman ρ=0.37 (weak)——两个模型本质上有不同的 vulnerability landscape。\n      Qwen3-32B 的 ρ=0.77 (moderate) 说明 scale 恢复了部分 alignment，但未完全收敛。\n      Binary effect 仍显著 (Qwen3-8B +23.7pp, p<0.0001)——ambiguity 对所有模型都有害，\n      但 \"哪种 ambiguity 更有害\" 取决于模型能力。\n\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      3,000 episodes 统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer effect,\n      C4 model×type interaction, power analysis, TOST, inter-model agreement, information delta control。\n    expected_results:\n      # C1: Binary effect (5-model pooled)\n      binary_effect_5model_pp: 30.2\n      binary_effect_5model_ci: \"[27.5, 32.9]\"\n      mcnemar_or_5model: 24.1\n      mcnemar_or_ci: \"[16.3, 35.6]\"\n      mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      per_type_all_significant: true\n      weakest_type_effect: \"coreferential +22.8pp (Qwen3-8B drags avg down from +16pp to... wait, UP — Qwen3-8B has high coreferential)\"\n      # C2: Type hierarchy (5-model pooled)\n      omnibus_chi2_5model: 18.7\n      omnibus_p_5model: 0.002\n      cramers_v_5model: 0.11\n      # Per-type 5-model pooled violation rates (ambiguous)\n      pooled_rates: {auth_scope: \"42.8%\", incompleteness: \"42.0%\", cp: \"30.4%\", scopal: \"35.8%\", lexical: \"33.4%\", coreferential: \"34.8%\"}\n      # C3: Layer effect (5-model pooled)\n      spec_avg_5model: \"38.4%\"\n      ling_avg_5model: \"34.7%\"\n      layer_gap_5model_pp: 3.7\n      layer_gap_ci: \"[-1.2, 8.6]\"\n      layer_gap_p: 0.14\n      # C4: Model × type interaction\n      model_type_interaction_chi2: 52.3\n      model_type_interaction_p: 0.008\n      model_type_interaction_v: 0.089\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.001\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.072\n      # Logistic regression: type×model interaction LRT\n      interaction_lrt_chi2: 38.6\n      interaction_lrt_p: 0.003\n      interaction_lrt_df: 20\n      # Per-model type rank correlation with GPT-5.4\n      rank_rho_gpt41: 0.94\n      rank_rho_claude: 0.54\n      rank_rho_qwen32b: 0.77\n      rank_rho_qwen8b: 0.37\n      # TOST equivalence\n      tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: \"6/15\"\n      tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: \"2/15\"\n      # Power analysis\n      mde_c2_v: 0.18\n      mde_c3_pp: 9.5\n      observed_c2_v: 0.11\n      observed_c3_gap: 3.7\n      # Inter-model agreement (Berry & Kamsties supplementary)\n      fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n      fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.85\n      same_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.58\n      different_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.42\n      # Information delta control variable\n      avg_token_delta_spec: 3.4\n      avg_token_delta_ling: 1.7\n      token_delta_violation_corr: 0.31\n      token_delta_partial_r_after_type: 0.14\n    result_rationale: >\n      C1 (+30.2pp, CI [27.5, 32.9]): 从 plan_002 的 +36.5pp 下降 6pp。\n      原因: Qwen3-8B 的弱 binary effect (+23.7pp) 和 Claude 的 (+26.5pp) 拉低 pooled 值。\n      但 CI 远离零，OR=24.1 仍 massive——文献中最大的 ambiguity → safety 因果效应。\n      Per-type 均显著 (最弱: CP +25.6pp)——\"所有 ambiguity 都 nocuous\" 成立。\n\n      C2 (V=0.11, p=0.002): omnibus χ² 显著说明 types 不完全等价，\n      但 V=0.11 (weak) 远低于 plan_002 2-model 的 V=0.207。\n      原因: open-source 模型的 reversed/flat profile 平均化了 type 间差异。\n      具体看: auth_scope/incompleteness 仍最高 (~43%)，但 coreferential 从 25% 跳至 34.8%\n      (Claude 42% + Qwen3-8B 45% 拉高)，压缩了原本的 range。\n      TOST: ±15pp 有 6/15 pairs equivalent (原 3/15)——更多 type pairs 在统计上不可区分。\n\n      C3 (gap 3.7pp, p=0.14, n.s.): layer gap 不显著。CI [-1.2, 8.6] 包含 0。\n      GPT 的 positive gap (~13pp) 被 Claude (-1pp) + Qwen3-8B (-8pp) 抵消。\n      MDE=9.5pp: 即使有 power，跨模型方向不一致使 pooled estimate 本身无 interpretive value。\n      Layer hierarchy 从 \"finding\" 变为 \"GPT-family tendency\"。\n\n      C4 (interaction p=0.008): worst tier 最 informative finding。\n      5×6 contingency table 中 model×type interaction 高度显著——type ranking 是 model-dependent。\n      Three distinct vulnerability profiles:\n      - GPT family: spec-sensitive (auth_scope/incompleteness peak)\n      - Claude: coreferential-sensitive (RLHF safety coverage gap)\n      - Qwen3-8B: ling-sensitive (surface heuristic dependence)\n      Spearman ρ gradient: GPT intra-family 0.94 > Qwen3-32B 0.77 > Claude 0.54 > Qwen3-8B 0.37\n\n      Inter-model Fleiss κ=0.62 (ambiguous) vs 0.85 (unambiguous):\n      分歧主要在 ambiguous clauses——ambiguity 暴露了 model-specific interpretation strategies。\n      58% same interpretation → 不是 true nocuity (divergent readings) 而是 systematic bias\n      (models differ in fallback strategies when they can't resolve ambiguity)。\n      Berry & Kamsties 框架下: 这是 \"systematic nocuity\" (所有模型都错但错法不同)\n      而非 \"divergent nocuity\" (不同解读)。\n\n      Token delta: spec-layer 3.4 vs ling-layer 1.7 tokens，与 violation rate 弱相关 (r=0.31)。\n      但 partial correlation after controlling for type = 0.14 (n.s.)——\n      token delta 不是 independent confound，与 type 共线。需 disclose 但不构成 fatal threat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"5-Model Pooled Per-Type Results\"\n        columns: [type, layer, amb_rate, unamb_rate, Δpp, \"95% CI\", \"per-type McNemar p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, spec, \"42.8%\", \"5.8%\", \"+37.0pp\", \"[31.2, 42.8]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [incompleteness, spec, \"42.0%\", \"5.4%\", \"+36.6pp\", \"[30.8, 42.4]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, spec, \"30.4%\", \"4.8%\", \"+25.6pp\", \"[20.1, 31.1]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [scopal, ling, \"35.8%\", \"5.6%\", \"+30.2pp\", \"[24.5, 35.9]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [lexical, ling, \"33.4%\", \"5.2%\", \"+28.2pp\", \"[22.6, 33.8]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [coreferential, ling, \"34.8%\", \"6.0%\", \"+28.8pp\", \"[23.1, 34.5]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n      - name: \"Layer Effect by Model\"\n        columns: [model, spec_avg, ling_avg, layer_gap_pp, direction]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, \"47.3%\", \"34.3%\", \"+13.0pp\", \"spec > ling\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, \"45.7%\", \"33.0%\", \"+12.7pp\", \"spec > ling\"]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, \"34.0%\", \"35.0%\", \"-1.0pp\", \"≈ flat (reversed)\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B-AWQ, \"37.3%\", \"35.3%\", \"+2.0pp\", \"≈ flat\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"27.7%\", \"35.7%\", \"-8.0pp\", \"ling > spec (reversed)\"]\n          - [5-model_pooled, \"38.4%\", \"34.7%\", \"+3.7pp\", \"n.s. (p=0.14)\"]\n      - name: \"Model × Type Interaction: Type Rank by Model (ambiguous violation rate)\"\n        columns: [rank, gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude, Qwen3-32B, Qwen3-8B]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1 (highest)\", auth_scope, auth_scope, coreferential, incompleteness, coreferential]\n          - [2, incompleteness, incompleteness, auth_scope, auth_scope, scopal]\n          - [3, scopal, scopal, incompleteness, coreferential, lexical]\n          - [4, lexical, lexical, scopal, scopal, incompleteness]\n          - [5, CP, CP, lexical, lexical, auth_scope]\n          - [\"6 (lowest)\", coreferential, coreferential, CP, CP, CP]\n      - name: \"Inter-Model Agreement (Berry & Kamsties Analysis)\"\n        columns: [metric, ambiguous, unambiguous, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [Fleiss_κ, 0.62, 0.85, \"moderate vs almost-perfect\"]\n          - [same_interpretation_pct, \"58%\", \"91%\", \"ambiguity drives divergence\"]\n          - [systematic_bias_pct, \"34%\", \"7%\", \"models differ in fallback strategy\"]\n          - [random_disagreement_pct, \"8%\", \"2%\", \"noise floor\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type 5-model pooled binary effect with 95% CI — C1 headline figure, all types significant\"\n      - \"Model×Type heatmap: 5 models × 6 types, color-coded — cross-pattern clearly visible\"\n      - \"Layer gap by model: bar chart with CI showing GPT positive, Qwen3-8B negative, others near zero\"\n      - \"Parallel coordinates: type rank across 5 models — lines crossing extensively (no stable ranking)\"\n      - \"Scatter: token delta vs violation rate per type, with partial regression line\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_004 是 worst tier 定性的核心。三个结论:\n      (1) C1 survives robustly: +30.2pp 是 massive causal effect, 6 types all significant, perturbation-backed。\n      (2) C2/C3 collapse: V=0.11 weak, layer gap n.s.——不能声称 universal type hierarchy。\n      但 interaction 显著 (p=0.008) 说明 types 确实 differently dangerous——只是 \"哪个更危险\" 是 model-dependent。\n      (3) C4 升级为 secondary finding: three vulnerability profiles (GPT spec-sensitive,\n      Claude coref-sensitive, Qwen8B ling-sensitive) 是 novel 且 practically relevant insight。\n      Reframe: layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      300 violation traces (50/type) 定性分析。Failure mode 分类、\n      跨层区分检验、ambiguity blindness 量化、model-specific pattern 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces_sampled: 300\n      # Failure mode distribution (pooled across types)\n      failure_modes:\n        assumption_based_action: \"38%\"\n        scope_misapplication: \"22%\"\n        conservative_refusal: \"15%\"\n        arbitrary_rule_selection: \"14%\"\n        permission_escalation: \"11%\"\n      # Cross-layer failure mode overlap\n      failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n      assumption_in_spec_pct: 40\n      assumption_in_ling_pct: 36\n      scope_misapplication_in_spec_pct: 18\n      scope_misapplication_in_ling_pct: 26\n      # Ambiguity blindness\n      explicit_ambiguity_mention_pct: 8\n      implicit_deliberation_pct: 20\n      surface_adoption_pct: 72\n      # Model-specific patterns\n      gpt54_assumption_pct: 45\n      gpt54_explicit_mention_pct: 12\n      claude_conservative_refusal_pct: 28\n      claude_explicit_mention_pct: 6\n      qwen8b_surface_adoption_pct: 85\n      qwen8b_explicit_mention_pct: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-layer failure mode overlap 42%: 如果 layer 是 deterministic predictor of failure mechanism，\n      match 应接近 80%+。实际仅 42% 说明 failure mode 不由 layer 决定。\n      \"Assumption-based action\" (遇到歧义直接假设一种解读并执行) 是 dominant mode，\n      且在两个 layer 上近乎等比例 (spec 40%, ling 36%)——\n      agent 的 failure mechanism 是 universal 的 \"guess and act\" 而非 type-specific misparse。\n\n      反直觉: scope_misapplication 在 ling-layer (26%) > spec-layer (18%)——\n      因为 scopal/coreferential 的 syntactic structure 确实触发更多 scope parsing error，\n      而 spec-layer 的 failure 更多是 \"assume permission exists\" (assumption-based)。\n      但这个差异不足以支撑 clean layer mechanism story——两个 layer 都有大量 assumption-based failures。\n\n      Ambiguity blindness: 92% traces 中 agent 未 meta-cognitively 识别歧义。\n      这是 universal 现象——所有模型所有 types 都展现。差异仅在 degree:\n      GPT-5.4 有 12% explicit mention (最高, 但仍极低)，Qwen3-8B 仅 2% (近乎完全 blind)。\n      Claude 的 conservative_refusal 28% (远高于平均) 解释了其低 auth_scope rate:\n      Claude refuse 而非 violate，但这不是 ambiguity awareness——\n      是 safety training 的 blanket conservatism，不区分 ambiguous vs unambiguous uncertainty。\n\n      Model-specific failure patterns 直接支撑 C4:\n      GPT 的 assumption_based 45% (aggressive interpretation) vs Claude 的 refusal 28%\n      (conservative) vs Qwen3-8B 的 surface_adoption 85% (uncritical execution)——\n      三种 distinct failure strategies，对应三种 vulnerability profiles。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Failure Mode Distribution by Layer\"\n        columns: [failure_mode, spec_layer, ling_layer, pooled, layer_specificity]\n        rows:\n          - [assumption_based_action, \"40%\", \"36%\", \"38%\", \"low (Δ=4pp)\"]\n          - [scope_misapplication, \"18%\", \"26%\", \"22%\", \"moderate (ling-biased)\"]\n          - [conservative_refusal, \"14%\", \"16%\", \"15%\", \"low (Δ=2pp)\"]\n          - [arbitrary_rule_selection, \"16%\", \"12%\", \"14%\", \"low (Δ=4pp)\"]\n          - [permission_escalation, \"12%\", \"10%\", \"11%\", \"low (Δ=2pp)\"]\n      - name: \"Ambiguity Awareness in Agent Traces by Model\"\n        columns: [awareness_level, gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude, Qwen3-32B, Qwen3-8B, pooled]\n        rows:\n          - [explicit_mention, \"12%\", \"10%\", \"6%\", \"5%\", \"2%\", \"8%\"]\n          - [implicit_deliberation, \"25%\", \"22%\", \"24%\", \"18%\", \"13%\", \"20%\"]\n          - [surface_adoption, \"63%\", \"68%\", \"70%\", \"77%\", \"85%\", \"72%\"]\n      - name: \"Failure Mode by Model\"\n        columns: [model, assumption_based, scope_misapplication, conservative_refusal, arbitrary_rule, permission_escalation]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, \"45%\", \"24%\", \"8%\", \"13%\", \"10%\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, \"42%\", \"23%\", \"10%\", \"15%\", \"10%\"]\n          - [claude, \"22%\", \"18%\", \"28%\", \"16%\", \"16%\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"38%\", \"22%\", \"14%\", \"14%\", \"12%\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"43%\", \"20%\", \"12%\", \"15%\", \"10%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sankey diagram: type → failure mode → outcome — 高度交叉流动，无 clean type→mode mapping\"\n      - \"Annotated trace pair: spec-layer (auth_scope) vs ling-layer (coreferential) 的 assumption-based action — 几乎 identical reasoning pattern\"\n      - \"Ambiguity blindness spectrum: 5 models 在 explicit↔surface 连续体上的位置\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis 无法支撑 layer-specific failure mechanism 叙事 (failure_mode_layer_match 仅 42%)，\n      但强力支撑 \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 作为 §6 核心:\n      92% traces 展现 blindness 是 universal 现象——所有模型在所有 type 上\n      都无法 meta-cognitively detect ambiguity。这连接 Ferreira 的 good-enough processing:\n      agents 对 grammatically fluent ambiguous clauses 做 shallow parse and act，\n      不触发 reanalysis/clarification。\n      Practical implication: 与其按 type 排序 (ranking model-dependent)，\n      不如投资 any-ambiguity detection——因为 agent 本身 blind to all types equally。\n      这完美 align reframe (C) binary effect + (B) blindness mechanism。\n\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes。\n      Test-retest ICC, bootstrap CI width。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 900\n      icc_overall: 0.68\n      icc_per_type: {auth_scope: 0.74, incompleteness: 0.72, cp: 0.65, scopal: 0.58, lexical: 0.63, coreferential: 0.48}\n      bootstrap_ci_width_binary_effect_pp: 11.5\n      bootstrap_ci_width_per_type_pp: 14.8\n      max_replicate_swing_pp: 12.3\n      max_swing_type: coreferential\n      icc_ambiguous_only: 0.65\n      icc_unambiguous_only: 0.79\n    result_rationale: >\n      Overall ICC 0.68 (moderate): 可接受但不 excellent。\n      Signature worst-tier pattern:\n      (a) Auth_scope/incompleteness 最 reliable (0.74/0.72): 高 violation rate type 的\n      absolute swing 对 ICC 影响较小 (±8pp on 43% base vs ±8pp on 35% base)。\n      (b) Coreferential 最 unreliable (0.48): 三重叠加效应——\n      clause 质量 (plan_001 pass_rate 0.88) × 跨模型行为异质 (Qwen3-8B 45% vs GPT 25%)\n      × API temperature sampling noise。这三者使 coreferential replicate variance 极大。\n      (c) Scopal ICC 0.58: 与 MVP→plan_002 的 51.7%→40% historical swing 一致。\n\n      Bootstrap CI width 11.5pp (binary effect) 超过 <10pp 理想阈值:\n      per-type CI width 14.8pp 更宽——type-level 比较 power 有限。\n      V=0.11 的 type effect 在此 noise level 下可能部分是 noise, 也可能被 noise 掩盖。\n      但 binary effect (30.2pp ÷ 11.5pp CI width = SNR 2.6) 仍 robust。\n\n      Unambiguous ICC 0.79 > ambiguous 0.65: ambiguous condition 的 variance 更大——\n      agent 在 ambiguous clause 上的 behavior 本身不稳定，进一步削弱 type-level precision。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"ICC by Type\"\n        columns: [type, ICC_ambiguous, ICC_unambiguous, ICC_combined, max_replicate_swing_pp]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.76, 0.82, 0.74, \"8.2pp\"]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.73, 0.80, 0.72, \"9.1pp\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, 0.67, 0.78, 0.65, \"10.5pp\"]\n          - [scopal, 0.60, 0.76, 0.58, \"11.8pp\"]\n          - [lexical, 0.64, 0.77, 0.63, \"10.2pp\"]\n          - [coreferential, 0.50, 0.72, 0.48, \"12.3pp\"]\n          - [overall, 0.70, 0.79, 0.68, \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ICC forest plot per type with 95% CI — coreferential CI 明显宽于其他 types\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reliability 数据进一步支撑 \"focus on binary, not type\":\n      binary effect reliability adequate (ICC 0.68 pooled, CI 11.5pp width on 30pp effect),\n      type-level reliability insufficient for fine-grained ranking claims\n      (coreferential ICC 0.48, CI 14.8pp width on ~5pp type differences)。\n      Coreferential 的低 reliability 是 compound 问题——clause quality + model heterogeneity + sampling noise。\n      Paper 需 explicitly discuss type-level measurement uncertainty。\n\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Synthetic clause linguistic properties vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities。\n      KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR。\n    expected_results:\n      ks_sentence_length: {statistic: 0.18, p: 0.12}\n      ks_parse_depth: {statistic: 0.21, p: 0.08}\n      ks_flesch_kincaid: {statistic: 0.14, p: 0.23}\n      ks_ttr: {statistic: 0.10, p: 0.41}\n      synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.2\n      drip_r_mean_tokens: 27.8\n      synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 3.1\n      drip_r_mean_parse_depth: 3.8\n      overall_verdict: acceptable\n      noted_difference: \"synthetic clauses slightly shorter and shallower parse trees — matched-pair design favors minimal pairs\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Realism validation 基本独立于 worst tier: clause 的语言学属性不受\n      downstream 实验结果影响。KS tests 大部分 n.s. (p>0.05)——\n      surface properties 分布相似。Parse depth 边界显著 (p=0.08):\n      synthetic clauses 稍简单因为 matched-pair design 倾向 minimal variation。\n      在 worst tier 下值得额外注意: 如果 synthetic clauses 系统性简单，\n      可能 underestimate real-world violation rate (更复杂的自然歧义可能更危险)。\n      但 +30pp binary effect 足够大，不太可能被此 bias 逆转。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R\"\n        columns: [property, synthetic_mean, DRIP-R_mean, KS_statistic, p_value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"sentence_length (tokens)\", 24.2, 27.8, 0.18, 0.12]\n          - [parse_depth, 3.1, 3.8, 0.21, 0.08]\n          - [Flesch-Kincaid, 12.4, 11.8, 0.14, 0.23]\n          - [type-token_ratio, 0.72, 0.70, 0.10, 0.41]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Distribution overlay: synthetic vs DRIP-R — sentence length and parse depth 有 visible but non-significant shift\"\n    analysis: >\n      Realism pass。Method 中 disclose parse depth 差异。\n      Reviewer RC4 应答充分: matched-pair design 本身需要 synthetic control,\n      linguistic properties 统计上与自然歧义不可区分。\n\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators, LLM judge 校准。\n      Worst tier: F1 < 0.75 for ≥2 types, type-specific bias 暴露。\n    expected_results:\n      human_annotator_kappa: 0.82\n      # Overall judge metrics\n      judge_overall_f1: 0.72\n      judge_overall_precision: 0.78\n      judge_overall_recall: 0.67\n      judge_overall_kappa_vs_human: 0.63\n      # Per-type judge F1\n      judge_f1_per_type: {auth_scope: 0.68, incompleteness: 0.76, cp: 0.79, scopal: 0.77, lexical: 0.74, coreferential: 0.61}\n      # Per-type bias direction\n      auth_scope_bias: \"under-detection: recall 0.56, precision 0.82 → misses subtle permission boundary crossings\"\n      coreferential_bias: \"over-detection: recall 0.64, precision 0.58 → flags legitimate info-gathering as violations\"\n      # Per-severity tier\n      judge_f1_tier1_critical: 0.82\n      judge_f1_tier2_moderate: 0.68\n      judge_f1_tier3_minor: 0.55\n      # Cross-judge asymmetry\n      claude_judged_by_gpt54_f1: 0.75\n      gpt54_judged_by_gpt41_f1: 0.69\n      cross_judge_asymmetry_pp: 6\n      # Bias-corrected rate estimates\n      auth_scope_corrected: \"+4-6pp (true rate likely ~47-49% not 42.8%)\"\n      coreferential_corrected: \"-5-8pp (true rate likely ~27-30% not 34.8%)\"\n      corrected_cramers_v_estimate: \"~0.14 (still weak)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge calibration 暴露 worst tier 最有破坏力的 measurement issue:\n\n      Coreferential F1=0.61: LLM judge over-detect coreferential violations。\n      原因: agent 在 RC attachment 歧义下采取的 \"exploratory query\" (查询哪个 entity 适用)\n      被 judge 误判为 \"unauthorized action\" (false positive)。\n      Judge 缺乏 human 的 pragmatic judgment——无法区分 \"agent 在探索性确认\" vs \"agent 在违规操作\"。\n      结果: coreferential reported rate (34.8%) 高估 ~5-8pp，真实 rate 可能 ~27-30%。\n\n      Auth_scope F1=0.68: judge under-detect auth_scope violations。\n      原因: auth_scope violation 常表现为 \"subtle permission boundary crossing\"——\n      agent 在模糊授权范围内行动，不明显违规 (如: 给客户 10% 折扣，policy 说 \"reasonable discount\"\n      但未定义 boundary)。Judge 倾向 \"不确定则判 non-violation\" → false negative。\n      结果: auth_scope reported rate (42.8%) 低估 ~4-6pp，真实 rate 可能 ~47-49%。\n\n      两个 bias 方向相互作用——恰好压缩了 type 间差异:\n      coreferential 高估 + auth_scope 低估 → 缩小 range → 降低 V 值。\n      Bias-corrected V 估计 ~0.14 (vs observed 0.11)——仍 weak, 不改变 \"type effect 弱\" 的结论，\n      但说明 raw V=0.11 有 measurement component。\n\n      Cross-judge asymmetry 6pp: Claude 被 gpt-5.4 (最强 judge) 判定 F1=0.75，\n      gpt-5.4 被 gpt-4.1 (较弱 judge) 判定仅 F1=0.69。\n      弱 judge 对强 model traces 更难准确判定——Method 必须 disclose。\n\n      Per-severity: tier-3 minor violations F1=0.55 (near random)——\n      judge 对 \"subtle/minor\" violations 几乎无法判定。\n      主要影响 severity-weighted analysis, binary violation/non-violation 受影响较小。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Judge Calibration by Type\"\n        columns: [type, precision, recall, F1, bias_direction, estimated_rate_correction]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.82, 0.56, 0.68, \"under-detection\", \"+4-6pp\"]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.80, 0.72, 0.76, \"slight under-detection\", \"+1-2pp\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, 0.81, 0.77, 0.79, \"balanced\", \"±1pp\"]\n          - [scopal, 0.79, 0.75, 0.77, \"balanced\", \"±1pp\"]\n          - [lexical, 0.76, 0.72, 0.74, \"slight over-detection\", \"-1-2pp\"]\n          - [coreferential, 0.58, 0.64, 0.61, \"over-detection\", \"-5-8pp\"]\n      - name: \"Judge Calibration by Severity Tier\"\n        columns: [severity, n_samples, precision, recall, F1]\n        rows:\n          - [tier-1_critical, 35, 0.85, 0.79, 0.82]\n          - [tier-2_moderate, 40, 0.73, 0.64, 0.68]\n          - [tier-3_minor, 25, 0.60, 0.51, 0.55]\n      - name: \"Cross-Judge Asymmetry\"\n        columns: [agent_model, judge_model, F1, note]\n        rows:\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, gpt-5.4, 0.75, \"strongest judge\"]\n          - [gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, 0.69, \"weaker judge on stronger agent\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, gpt-5.4, 0.78, \"strongest judge on mid-tier agent\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, gpt-5.4, 0.71, \"open-source traces harder to judge\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix per type: coreferential FP 区域和 auth_scope FN 区域突出标记\"\n      - \"Calibration curve: judge confidence vs human agreement — coreferential 偏离对角线最远\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration 是 worst tier 的第二个 structural threat (after model×type interaction)。\n      F1<0.75 for coreferential (0.61) + auth_scope (0.68) 直接削弱这两个 type 的数值可信度。\n      Paper 必须: (a) report calibration as standard practice, (b) provide bias-corrected estimates,\n      (c) flag coreferential/auth_scope absolute values as measurement-sensitive,\n      (d) disclose cross-judge asymmetry in Method。\n      Silver lining: binary effect 的 calibration 尚可 (overall F1=0.72, tier-1 F1=0.82)，\n      C1 headline number 受影响最小。bias-corrected V ~0.14 仍 weak——\n      measurement correction 不改变 \"type hierarchy 不 robust\" 的 worst-tier 结论。\n\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。\n      Fine-tune on 240 pairs, eval on 60 held-out。\n    expected_results:\n      model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n      train_size: 240\n      test_size: 60\n      test_f1: 0.78\n      test_precision: 0.81\n      test_recall: 0.75\n      per_type_f1: {auth_scope: 0.82, incompleteness: 0.80, cp: 0.76, scopal: 0.79, lexical: 0.77, coreferential: 0.72}\n      training_epochs: 5\n      best_epoch: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      F1=0.78 是 reasonable PoC 水平: 证明 binary ambiguity detection 是 feasible NLP task，\n      但远未 production-ready。Coreferential F1 最低 (0.72) 与 judge calibration (0.61)\n      和 reliability (ICC 0.48) 的 pattern 一致: coreferential 是最难检测/判定的 type。\n\n      在 worst tier reframe 下，classifier PoC 强化 reframe (C):\n      \"任何 ambiguity detection (甚至 binary) 都有巨大安全收益\"——\n      F1=0.78 的 binary detector 在 +30pp violation rate gap 上\n      可提供 meaningful early warning。Type-specific detection 既不必要\n      (type ranking model-dependent) 也不额外有价值 (binary 已覆盖核心风险)。\n      这恰好与 worst tier 结论 align: binary detection = high ROI, type triage = low ROI。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Classifier PoC Performance\"\n        columns: [metric, overall, auth_scope, incomp, CP, scopal, lexical, coref]\n        rows:\n          - [F1, 0.78, 0.82, 0.80, 0.76, 0.79, 0.77, 0.72]\n          - [Precision, 0.81, 0.85, 0.83, 0.78, 0.82, 0.80, 0.74]\n          - [Recall, 0.75, 0.79, 0.77, 0.74, 0.76, 0.74, 0.70]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-type F1 bar chart: coreferential 最低, auth_scope 最高\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix: false negatives 集中在 coreferential 和 CP\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC 在 worst tier 下反而 perfectly narrative-aligned:\n      binary detection feasible (F1=0.78), type-specific pipeline 不必要\n      (type ranking 本身 model-dependent)。Practical contribution 的 optimal framing:\n      投资 binary detector 而非 type-specific triage pipeline。\n      与 C1 massive binary effect + ambiguity blindness 形成 coherent practical story。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":27054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":23,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6d87fd7e-4fd2-4879-997a-f48c2624ff14","uuid":"ae13e453-3dc4-4a76-b743-9fee1e721ad5"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":699093,"duration_api_ms":700750,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  Layer hierarchy 无法作为 headline claim。5-model pooled layer gap 仅 ~4pp (p=0.14, n.s.)，\n  被 model×type interaction (p=0.008) 瓦解——type ranking 因模型架构而异\n  (GPT 系 spec>ling, Qwen3-8B 反转, Claude 混合)。Judge calibration 暴露\n  coreferential (F1=0.61) 和 auth_scope (F1=0.68) 的 type-specific measurement bias，\n  进一步削弱 type-level claims。Error analysis failure mode 跨层重叠 42%，无 clean mechanism 区分。\n  首选 reframe: (C) \"The Massive Binary Effect\" 为 primary——+30pp 仍是文献最大因果效应 +\n  perturbation control PASS (Δ=4.2pp, ratio=0.13)；(B) \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 为 §6 核心——\n  92% traces 中 agent 未识别歧义存在，universal across types and models。\n  C2 降级为 \"Model-Dependent Vulnerability Profiles\" (model×type interaction 从 nuisance 升级为 finding)；\n  C3 layer claim 放弃。备选标题: \"Policy Ambiguity Causes Catastrophic Safety Violations\n  in LLM Agents: A Causal Study\"。仍投 EMNLP——C1 (causal binary effect) +\n  perturbation control + ambiguity blindness analysis = solid 3-contribution paper。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n\n  - name: full_study_clause_generation\n    plan_id: plan_001\n    description: >\n      生成 140 新 clause pairs (coreferential 50, auth_scope 50, lexical +20, incompleteness +20)，\n      补全 6 types × 50 pairs = 300 对。混合 CP 格式 (labeled + unlabeled)。Chantree-style 质量验证。\n    expected_results:\n      total_pairs: 300\n      pairs_per_type: 50\n      cp_labeled_ratio: 0.50\n      quality_pass_rate: 0.92\n      avg_token_delta_amb_vs_unamb: 3.8\n      coreferential_revision_rounds: 3\n      auth_scope_revision_rounds: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Clause 生成本身不受 worst tier 影响——数据准备阶段。但 quality_pass_rate 92% 而非 >95%\n      因为 coreferential 的 RC attachment 与 scopal 存在边界重叠 (RC8 预示的问题)，\n      以及 auth_scope 与 incompleteness 的 distinction 需要精细控制 (RC9)。\n      Coreferential 需要 3 轮修订 (vs 常规 1-2 轮)：mini-pilot 会暴露 2/5 clauses 触发\n      conservative refusal 而非 violation，需重写。这些 clause 层面的质量差异\n      会在后续实验中放大为 type-specific measurement noise。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Clause Pair Statistics by Type\"\n        columns: [type, n_pairs, avg_amb_tokens, avg_unamb_tokens, token_delta, quality_pass_rate]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 50, 28.3, 32.1, 3.8, 0.90]\n          - [incompleteness, 50, 26.7, 30.5, 3.8, 0.94]\n          - [conditional_polysemy, 50, 24.2, 25.8, 1.6, 0.96]\n          - [scopal, 50, 22.5, 23.9, 1.4, 0.96]\n          - [lexical, 50, 21.8, 23.1, 1.3, 0.94]\n          - [coreferential, 50, 25.1, 27.4, 2.3, 0.88]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Token length distribution per type (box plot): spec-layer types 系统性更长，unambiguous 版本需更多 explicit information\"\n    analysis: >\n      Coreferential quality_pass_rate 最低 (0.88)，auth_scope 0.90——这两个新 type 的 clause\n      质量问题会在 plan_009 judge calibration 中以 type-specific F1 下降的形式体现。\n      Token delta spec-layer (3.8) > ling-layer (1.7) 是 potential confound，\n      plan_004 需 report 并控制。\n\n  - name: new_type_mini_pilot\n    plan_id: plan_001b\n    description: >\n      Coreferential + auth_scope 各 5 clauses × 2 conditions × 1 model (gpt-5.4) = 20 episodes。\n      验证新类型基本可行性。\n    expected_results:\n      coreferential_amb_violation_rate: 0.40\n      coreferential_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      auth_scope_amb_violation_rate: 0.60\n      auth_scope_unamb_violation_rate: 0.00\n      coreferential_binary_effect_pp: 40\n      auth_scope_binary_effect_pp: 60\n      systematic_issues_found: true\n      issues_detail: \"2/5 coreferential clauses 触发 conservative refusal 而非 violation; 1/5 auth_scope unambiguous 版本仍残余歧义\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Mini-pilot 在 gpt-5.4 上给出 \"go\" 信号——两个新 type 均触发 violations，control < 15%。\n      但这是 worst tier 的隐患起点: gpt-5.4 的 auth_scope 60% / coreferential 40% pattern\n      看似 confirm spec > ling hierarchy，但 N=5 的 CI 极宽 (±30pp)。\n      关键: 相同 clauses 在 Qwen3-8B 上 profile 会反转 (coreferential ~45%, auth_scope ~28%)——\n      mini-pilot 仅测 1 model 无法预见跨模型 interaction。\n      gpt-5.4 上 coreferential 2/5 conservative refusal 预示该 type 行为异质性高，\n      但在 mini-pilot 被归为 \"fixable clause quality issue\" 而非 structural warning。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Mini-Pilot Results\"\n        columns: [type, condition, n, violations, rate]\n        rows:\n          - [coreferential, ambiguous, 5, 2, \"40%\"]\n          - [coreferential, unambiguous, 5, 0, \"0%\"]\n          - [auth_scope, ambiguous, 5, 3, \"60%\"]\n          - [auth_scope, unambiguous, 5, 0, \"0%\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      Mini-pilot 的 \"go\" 信号在 worst tier 下是 misleading confidence:\n      gpt-5.4 single-model validation 无法检测 model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n      实际需要 ≥2 model families 的 mini-pilot 才能预见 plan_003 的 interaction 问题。\n\n  - name: perturbation_control\n    plan_id: plan_010\n    description: >\n      30 non-ambiguity perturbation pairs (15 synonym substitution + 15 clause reordering)\n      × 2 conditions × 3 API models = 180 episodes。验证 ambiguity-specific 因果性。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 180\n      perturbation_delta_pp: 4.2\n      perturbation_ci: \"[-1.8, 10.2]\"\n      ambiguity_delta_pp: 31.5\n      ambiguity_ci: \"[26.8, 36.2]\"\n      net_delta_pp: 27.3\n      ratio: 0.13\n      verdict: PASS\n      synonym_substitution_delta_pp: 3.1\n      synonym_ci: \"[-3.2, 9.4]\"\n      clause_reordering_delta_pp: 5.3\n      clause_reordering_ci: \"[-0.8, 11.4]\"\n      ci_width_perturbation: 12.0\n    result_rationale: >\n      Perturbation control 在 worst tier 下仍 PASS——binary effect 的因果性不受 layer hierarchy 问题影响。\n      Δ_perturb=4.2pp (CI 含 0): synonym substitution (3.1pp) 和 clause reordering (5.3pp)\n      均不引起 meaningful violation rate 变化。Ratio=0.13 < 0.15 → PASS 最强形式。\n      Clause reordering 略高 (5.3pp) 源于轻微 primacy/recency effect，但远小于 ambiguity effect。\n      CI width 12.0pp 接近但未超过 15pp 追加阈值——worst tier 下这是 marginal 风险，\n      但当前数据足够。这个 PASS 是 worst tier 的最大 silver lining:\n      即使 type hierarchy 崩溃，binary ambiguity effect 仍有最强因果证据支撑，\n      使 reframe (C) \"Massive Binary Effect\" 有坚实因果基础。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Perturbation Control Results\"\n        columns: [condition, violation_rate, Δpp_vs_baseline, \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [unambiguous_baseline, \"5.5%\", \"—\", \"—\"]\n          - [synonym_substitution, \"8.6%\", \"+3.1pp\", \"[-3.2, 9.4]\"]\n          - [clause_reordering, \"10.8%\", \"+5.3pp\", \"[-0.8, 11.4]\"]\n          - [perturbation_pooled, \"9.7%\", \"+4.2pp\", \"[-1.8, 10.2]\"]\n          - [ambiguous, \"37.0%\", \"+31.5pp\", \"[26.8, 36.2]\"]\n      - name: \"Perturbation Verdict Summary\"\n        columns: [metric, value, threshold, verdict]\n        rows:\n          - [Δ_perturb, \"4.2pp\", \"< 5pp\", \"✓ PASS\"]\n          - [ratio, \"0.13\", \"< 0.15\", \"✓ PASS\"]\n          - [CI_contains_0, \"yes\", \"required\", \"✓\"]\n          - [CI_width, \"12.0pp\", \"< 15pp\", \"✓ (marginal)\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Bar chart: baseline / perturbation / ambiguity 三条件 violation rate + CI — ambiguity 远超其余两条件\"\n    analysis: >\n      PASS verdict 确保 C1 因果 claim 在任何 tier 下成立。\n      这是 paper 的 methodological backbone——区别于所有 prior work (DRIP-R, PhantomPolicy 均无此控制)。\n\n  - name: full_study_api\n    plan_id: plan_002\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 3 API models (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6) = 1,800 episodes。\n      在原 2-model 基础上新增 Claude。Cross-judge evaluation。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1800\n      # Per-model per-type violation rates (ambiguous condition)\n      gpt54_rates: {auth_scope: 0.55, incompleteness: 0.52, cp: 0.35, scopal: 0.40, lexical: 0.38, coreferential: 0.25}\n      gpt41_rates: {auth_scope: 0.53, incompleteness: 0.50, cp: 0.34, scopal: 0.39, lexical: 0.36, coreferential: 0.24}\n      claude_rates: {auth_scope: 0.38, incompleteness: 0.36, cp: 0.28, scopal: 0.33, lexical: 0.30, coreferential: 0.42}\n      # Per-model binary effects\n      gpt54_binary_effect_pp: 36.2\n      gpt41_binary_effect_pp: 34.0\n      claude_binary_effect_pp: 26.5\n      # Per-model layer gaps\n      gpt54_layer_gap_pp: 13.0\n      gpt41_layer_gap_pp: 12.7\n      claude_layer_gap_pp: -1.0\n      # Pooled 3-API metrics\n      binary_effect_3api_pp: 32.7\n      layer_gap_3api_pp: 8.2\n      cramers_v_3api: 0.15\n      model_main_effect_p_3api: 0.004\n      model_type_interaction_p_3api: 0.018\n      avg_unamb_rate_3api: 0.055\n      # Claude specifics\n      claude_unamb_rate: 0.080\n      claude_amb_avg: 0.345\n    result_rationale: >\n      GPT 系 (gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1) 复现 plan_002 原始 pattern: spec >> ling，两模型高度一致\n      (rank ρ=0.94)。GPT 对 authorization boundary 和 incompleteness 的 pragmatic underspecification\n      高度敏感——缺乏 explicit permission 时倾向 assume-and-act。\n\n      Claude 展现截然不同的 vulnerability profile——worst tier 的第一个转折点:\n      (a) auth_scope/incompleteness 显著低 (38%/36% vs GPT 55%/52%): Claude RLHF 训练\n      强化了 \"不确定时 refuse\" 的行为，specification-layer ambiguity 更多触发 refusal 而非 violation。\n      (b) coreferential 显著高 (42% vs GPT 25%): Claude 在 RC attachment 歧义上\n      系统性选择 wider-scope interpretation (执行而非收窄)。RC attachment 不触发 Claude 的\n      safety refusal mechanism (与 auth boundary 不同)，因此 Claude 在此 \"放松警惕\"。\n      (c) 结果: Claude layer gap 反转 (ling 35.0% > spec 34.0%)。\n      3-API pooled layer gap 从 2-model 的 19pp 压缩至 8.2pp。\n\n      Model×type interaction 已在 3 API 模型中显著 (p=0.018)——\n      尚未加入 Qwen 就已可见 type ranking 非 universal。\n      Claude binary effect 仅 +26.5pp: 整体更保守 (unamb baseline 8% vs GPT ~4.5%),\n      ambiguous 条件下更多 refuse/ask 而非 violate。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Ambiguous Condition)\"\n        columns: [type, layer, gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude-sonnet-4-6, 3-API_pooled]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, spec, \"55%\", \"53%\", \"38%\", \"48.7%\"]\n          - [incompleteness, spec, \"52%\", \"50%\", \"36%\", \"46.0%\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, spec, \"35%\", \"34%\", \"28%\", \"32.3%\"]\n          - [scopal, ling, \"40%\", \"39%\", \"33%\", \"37.3%\"]\n          - [lexical, ling, \"38%\", \"36%\", \"30%\", \"34.7%\"]\n          - [coreferential, ling, \"25%\", \"24%\", \"42%\", \"30.3%\"]\n          - [spec_avg, \"—\", \"47.3%\", \"45.7%\", \"34.0%\", \"42.3%\"]\n          - [ling_avg, \"—\", \"34.3%\", \"33.0%\", \"35.0%\", \"34.1%\"]\n          - [layer_gap, \"—\", \"+13.0pp\", \"+12.7pp\", \"-1.0pp\", \"+8.2pp\"]\n      - name: \"Binary Effect by API Model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, Δpp, McNemar_OR, p]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, \"40.8%\", \"4.6%\", \"+36.2pp\", 38.5, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, \"39.3%\", \"5.3%\", \"+34.0pp\", 31.2, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, \"34.5%\", \"8.0%\", \"+26.5pp\", 16.8, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [3-API_pooled, \"38.2%\", \"5.5%\", \"+32.7pp\", 28.4, \"<0.0001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap 3×6: 清晰显示 Claude coreferential 异常高 (42%) 与 auth_scope 异常低 (38%)——与 GPT 系对角相反\"\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type binary effect by model with 95% CI — Claude CI 与 GPT 不重叠 (auth_scope, coreferential)\"\n    analysis: >\n      Claude 的加入将 3-API layer gap 压缩至 8.2pp (从 2-model 19pp)。\n      model×type interaction 已显著 (p=0.018)——plan_003 加入 Qwen 后会进一步恶化。\n      Claude 的 coreferential 高 rate 机制: RLHF 的 safety training 覆盖了 authorization-class\n      violations 但不覆盖 referential-class misinterpretation，导致 asymmetric vulnerability。\n      C3 (universal layer hierarchy) 在此阶段已不可维持。\n\n  - name: full_study_local\n    plan_id: plan_003\n    description: >\n      300 clauses × 2 conditions × 2 local models (Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ via vLLM) = 1,200 episodes。\n      48 GPU-hours on RTX PRO 6000。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 1200\n      # Qwen3-8B per-type (ambiguous condition)\n      qwen8b_rates: {auth_scope: 0.28, incompleteness: 0.30, cp: 0.25, scopal: 0.32, lexical: 0.30, coreferential: 0.45}\n      qwen8b_binary_effect_pp: 23.7\n      qwen8b_unamb_rate: 0.080\n      qwen8b_amb_avg: 0.317\n      qwen8b_layer_gap_pp: -8.0\n      qwen8b_spec_avg: 0.277\n      qwen8b_ling_avg: 0.357\n      # Qwen3-32B-AWQ per-type (ambiguous condition)\n      qwen32b_rates: {auth_scope: 0.40, incompleteness: 0.42, cp: 0.30, scopal: 0.35, lexical: 0.33, coreferential: 0.38}\n      qwen32b_binary_effect_pp: 30.3\n      qwen32b_unamb_rate: 0.060\n      qwen32b_amb_avg: 0.363\n      qwen32b_layer_gap_pp: 2.0\n      qwen32b_spec_avg: 0.373\n      qwen32b_ling_avg: 0.353\n      # Pooled 2-local metrics\n      binary_effect_2local_pp: 27.0\n      layer_gap_2local_pp: -3.0\n      model_type_interaction_2local_p: 0.041\n    result_rationale: >\n      Qwen3-8B 是 worst tier 的关键变量——vulnerability profile 质变:\n\n      (a) Auth_scope 仅 28% (GPT-5.4 的一半): 8B 参数模型缺乏 pragmatic reasoning 能力，\n      无法 \"推断\" implicit permission boundary 并据此行动——不是因为保守 refuse (像 Claude)，\n      而是因为根本不理解 authorization 的 pragmatic implication，倾向 ignore 或 default 行为。\n      低 auth_scope violation ≠ 安全，只是不同的 failure mode (inaction vs wrong action)。\n\n      (b) Coreferential 高达 45% (GPT-5.4 的 1.8 倍): 小模型更依赖 surface syntactic heuristics\n      (如 left-attachment bias for RC)。GPT-5.4 能利用 tool response 做部分 disambiguation\n      (Berry & Kamsties 的 \"disambiguation channel\")，Qwen3-8B 不具备此能力——\n      对 linguistic-layer 反而更脆弱。\n\n      (c) Layer gap 反转至 -8pp (ling 35.7% > spec 27.7%): 完全颠覆 GPT 的 spec > ling pattern。\n      机制: 小模型的 pragmatic processing 不足使 spec-layer 失去 \"特别危险\" 的地位，\n      而 syntactic processing 的 surface heuristic 依赖使 ling-layer 变得更危险。\n\n      Qwen3-32B-AWQ 居中 (gap +2pp, nearly flat): scale 部分恢复了 spec-layer sensitivity，\n      但未达 GPT 水平。AWQ 4-bit 量化可能引入额外 noise 但不改变 qualitative pattern。\n      这支持 \"layer gap 是 emergent capability\"——需要足够的 pragmatic reasoning 能力\n      才能 \"解锁\" specification-layer 的特殊危险性。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Per-Model Per-Type Violation Rates (Local Models, Ambiguous)\"\n        columns: [type, layer, Qwen3-8B, Qwen3-32B-AWQ, 2-local_pooled]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, spec, \"28%\", \"40%\", \"34.0%\"]\n          - [incompleteness, spec, \"30%\", \"42%\", \"36.0%\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, spec, \"25%\", \"30%\", \"27.5%\"]\n          - [scopal, ling, \"32%\", \"35%\", \"33.5%\"]\n          - [lexical, ling, \"30%\", \"33%\", \"31.5%\"]\n          - [coreferential, ling, \"45%\", \"38%\", \"41.5%\"]\n          - [spec_avg, \"—\", \"27.7%\", \"37.3%\", \"32.5%\"]\n          - [ling_avg, \"—\", \"35.7%\", \"35.3%\", \"35.5%\"]\n          - [layer_gap, \"—\", \"-8.0pp\", \"+2.0pp\", \"-3.0pp\"]\n      - name: \"Binary Effect by Local Model\"\n        columns: [model, amb_rate, unamb_rate, Δpp, McNemar_OR, p]\n        rows:\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"31.7%\", \"8.0%\", \"+23.7pp\", 9.4, \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B-AWQ, \"36.3%\", \"6.0%\", \"+30.3pp\", 21.7, \"<0.0001\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Radar chart 5 models × 6 types: Qwen3-8B profile 与 GPT 系近似镜像——coreferential 峰值、auth_scope 谷底\"\n      - \"Layer gap by model bar chart: GPT 正、Claude/Qwen3-32B 近零、Qwen3-8B 负——gradient 随 model capability\"\n    analysis: >\n      Qwen3-8B 的 reversed layer profile 是 worst tier 的 smoking gun。\n      与 GPT-5.4 的 type rank Spearman ρ=0.37 (weak)——两个模型本质上有不同的 vulnerability landscape。\n      Qwen3-32B 的 ρ=0.77 (moderate) 说明 scale 恢复了部分 alignment，但未完全收敛。\n      Binary effect 仍显著 (Qwen3-8B +23.7pp, p<0.0001)——ambiguity 对所有模型都有害，\n      但 \"哪种 ambiguity 更有害\" 取决于模型能力。\n\n  - name: full_study_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_004\n    description: >\n      3,000 episodes 统计分析: C1 binary effect, C2 type hierarchy, C3 layer effect,\n      C4 model×type interaction, power analysis, TOST, inter-model agreement, information delta control。\n    expected_results:\n      # C1: Binary effect (5-model pooled)\n      binary_effect_5model_pp: 30.2\n      binary_effect_5model_ci: \"[27.5, 32.9]\"\n      mcnemar_or_5model: 24.1\n      mcnemar_or_ci: \"[16.3, 35.6]\"\n      mcnemar_p: \"<0.0001\"\n      per_type_all_significant: true\n      weakest_type_effect: \"coreferential +22.8pp (Qwen3-8B drags avg down from +16pp to... wait, UP — Qwen3-8B has high coreferential)\"\n      # C2: Type hierarchy (5-model pooled)\n      omnibus_chi2_5model: 18.7\n      omnibus_p_5model: 0.002\n      cramers_v_5model: 0.11\n      # Per-type 5-model pooled violation rates (ambiguous)\n      pooled_rates: {auth_scope: \"42.8%\", incompleteness: \"42.0%\", cp: \"30.4%\", scopal: \"35.8%\", lexical: \"33.4%\", coreferential: \"34.8%\"}\n      # C3: Layer effect (5-model pooled)\n      spec_avg_5model: \"38.4%\"\n      ling_avg_5model: \"34.7%\"\n      layer_gap_5model_pp: 3.7\n      layer_gap_ci: \"[-1.2, 8.6]\"\n      layer_gap_p: 0.14\n      # C4: Model × type interaction\n      model_type_interaction_chi2: 52.3\n      model_type_interaction_p: 0.008\n      model_type_interaction_v: 0.089\n      model_main_effect_p: 0.001\n      model_main_effect_v: 0.072\n      # Logistic regression: type×model interaction LRT\n      interaction_lrt_chi2: 38.6\n      interaction_lrt_p: 0.003\n      interaction_lrt_df: 20\n      # Per-model type rank correlation with GPT-5.4\n      rank_rho_gpt41: 0.94\n      rank_rho_claude: 0.54\n      rank_rho_qwen32b: 0.77\n      rank_rho_qwen8b: 0.37\n      # TOST equivalence\n      tost_15pp_equivalent_pairs: \"6/15\"\n      tost_10pp_equivalent_pairs: \"2/15\"\n      # Power analysis\n      mde_c2_v: 0.18\n      mde_c3_pp: 9.5\n      observed_c2_v: 0.11\n      observed_c3_gap: 3.7\n      # Inter-model agreement (Berry & Kamsties supplementary)\n      fleiss_kappa_ambiguous: 0.62\n      fleiss_kappa_unambiguous: 0.85\n      same_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.58\n      different_interpretation_pct_ambiguous: 0.42\n      # Information delta control variable\n      avg_token_delta_spec: 3.4\n      avg_token_delta_ling: 1.7\n      token_delta_violation_corr: 0.31\n      token_delta_partial_r_after_type: 0.14\n    result_rationale: >\n      C1 (+30.2pp, CI [27.5, 32.9]): 从 plan_002 的 +36.5pp 下降 6pp。\n      原因: Qwen3-8B 的弱 binary effect (+23.7pp) 和 Claude 的 (+26.5pp) 拉低 pooled 值。\n      但 CI 远离零，OR=24.1 仍 massive——文献中最大的 ambiguity → safety 因果效应。\n      Per-type 均显著 (最弱: CP +25.6pp)——\"所有 ambiguity 都 nocuous\" 成立。\n\n      C2 (V=0.11, p=0.002): omnibus χ² 显著说明 types 不完全等价，\n      但 V=0.11 (weak) 远低于 plan_002 2-model 的 V=0.207。\n      原因: open-source 模型的 reversed/flat profile 平均化了 type 间差异。\n      具体看: auth_scope/incompleteness 仍最高 (~43%)，但 coreferential 从 25% 跳至 34.8%\n      (Claude 42% + Qwen3-8B 45% 拉高)，压缩了原本的 range。\n      TOST: ±15pp 有 6/15 pairs equivalent (原 3/15)——更多 type pairs 在统计上不可区分。\n\n      C3 (gap 3.7pp, p=0.14, n.s.): layer gap 不显著。CI [-1.2, 8.6] 包含 0。\n      GPT 的 positive gap (~13pp) 被 Claude (-1pp) + Qwen3-8B (-8pp) 抵消。\n      MDE=9.5pp: 即使有 power，跨模型方向不一致使 pooled estimate 本身无 interpretive value。\n      Layer hierarchy 从 \"finding\" 变为 \"GPT-family tendency\"。\n\n      C4 (interaction p=0.008): worst tier 最 informative finding。\n      5×6 contingency table 中 model×type interaction 高度显著——type ranking 是 model-dependent。\n      Three distinct vulnerability profiles:\n      - GPT family: spec-sensitive (auth_scope/incompleteness peak)\n      - Claude: coreferential-sensitive (RLHF safety coverage gap)\n      - Qwen3-8B: ling-sensitive (surface heuristic dependence)\n      Spearman ρ gradient: GPT intra-family 0.94 > Qwen3-32B 0.77 > Claude 0.54 > Qwen3-8B 0.37\n\n      Inter-model Fleiss κ=0.62 (ambiguous) vs 0.85 (unambiguous):\n      分歧主要在 ambiguous clauses——ambiguity 暴露了 model-specific interpretation strategies。\n      58% same interpretation → 不是 true nocuity (divergent readings) 而是 systematic bias\n      (models differ in fallback strategies when they can't resolve ambiguity)。\n      Berry & Kamsties 框架下: 这是 \"systematic nocuity\" (所有模型都错但错法不同)\n      而非 \"divergent nocuity\" (不同解读)。\n\n      Token delta: spec-layer 3.4 vs ling-layer 1.7 tokens，与 violation rate 弱相关 (r=0.31)。\n      但 partial correlation after controlling for type = 0.14 (n.s.)——\n      token delta 不是 independent confound，与 type 共线。需 disclose 但不构成 fatal threat。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"5-Model Pooled Per-Type Results\"\n        columns: [type, layer, amb_rate, unamb_rate, Δpp, \"95% CI\", \"per-type McNemar p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, spec, \"42.8%\", \"5.8%\", \"+37.0pp\", \"[31.2, 42.8]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [incompleteness, spec, \"42.0%\", \"5.4%\", \"+36.6pp\", \"[30.8, 42.4]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, spec, \"30.4%\", \"4.8%\", \"+25.6pp\", \"[20.1, 31.1]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [scopal, ling, \"35.8%\", \"5.6%\", \"+30.2pp\", \"[24.5, 35.9]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [lexical, ling, \"33.4%\", \"5.2%\", \"+28.2pp\", \"[22.6, 33.8]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n          - [coreferential, ling, \"34.8%\", \"6.0%\", \"+28.8pp\", \"[23.1, 34.5]\", \"<0.0001\"]\n      - name: \"Layer Effect by Model\"\n        columns: [model, spec_avg, ling_avg, layer_gap_pp, direction]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, \"47.3%\", \"34.3%\", \"+13.0pp\", \"spec > ling\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, \"45.7%\", \"33.0%\", \"+12.7pp\", \"spec > ling\"]\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, \"34.0%\", \"35.0%\", \"-1.0pp\", \"≈ flat (reversed)\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B-AWQ, \"37.3%\", \"35.3%\", \"+2.0pp\", \"≈ flat\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"27.7%\", \"35.7%\", \"-8.0pp\", \"ling > spec (reversed)\"]\n          - [5-model_pooled, \"38.4%\", \"34.7%\", \"+3.7pp\", \"n.s. (p=0.14)\"]\n      - name: \"Model × Type Interaction: Type Rank by Model (ambiguous violation rate)\"\n        columns: [rank, gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude, Qwen3-32B, Qwen3-8B]\n        rows:\n          - [\"1 (highest)\", auth_scope, auth_scope, coreferential, incompleteness, coreferential]\n          - [2, incompleteness, incompleteness, auth_scope, auth_scope, scopal]\n          - [3, scopal, scopal, incompleteness, coreferential, lexical]\n          - [4, lexical, lexical, scopal, scopal, incompleteness]\n          - [5, CP, CP, lexical, lexical, auth_scope]\n          - [\"6 (lowest)\", coreferential, coreferential, CP, CP, CP]\n      - name: \"Inter-Model Agreement (Berry & Kamsties Analysis)\"\n        columns: [metric, ambiguous, unambiguous, interpretation]\n        rows:\n          - [Fleiss_κ, 0.62, 0.85, \"moderate vs almost-perfect\"]\n          - [same_interpretation_pct, \"58%\", \"91%\", \"ambiguity drives divergence\"]\n          - [systematic_bias_pct, \"34%\", \"7%\", \"models differ in fallback strategy\"]\n          - [random_disagreement_pct, \"8%\", \"2%\", \"noise floor\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: per-type 5-model pooled binary effect with 95% CI — C1 headline figure, all types significant\"\n      - \"Model×Type heatmap: 5 models × 6 types, color-coded — cross-pattern clearly visible\"\n      - \"Layer gap by model: bar chart with CI showing GPT positive, Qwen3-8B negative, others near zero\"\n      - \"Parallel coordinates: type rank across 5 models — lines crossing extensively (no stable ranking)\"\n      - \"Scatter: token delta vs violation rate per type, with partial regression line\"\n    analysis: >\n      Plan_004 是 worst tier 定性的核心。三个结论:\n      (1) C1 survives robustly: +30.2pp 是 massive causal effect, 6 types all significant, perturbation-backed。\n      (2) C2/C3 collapse: V=0.11 weak, layer gap n.s.——不能声称 universal type hierarchy。\n      但 interaction 显著 (p=0.008) 说明 types 确实 differently dangerous——只是 \"哪个更危险\" 是 model-dependent。\n      (3) C4 升级为 secondary finding: three vulnerability profiles (GPT spec-sensitive,\n      Claude coref-sensitive, Qwen8B ling-sensitive) 是 novel 且 practically relevant insight。\n      Reframe: layer hierarchy → model-dependent vulnerability profiles。\n\n  - name: error_analysis\n    plan_id: plan_005\n    description: >\n      300 violation traces (50/type) 定性分析。Failure mode 分类、\n      跨层区分检验、ambiguity blindness 量化、model-specific pattern 分析。\n    expected_results:\n      total_traces_sampled: 300\n      # Failure mode distribution (pooled across types)\n      failure_modes:\n        assumption_based_action: \"38%\"\n        scope_misapplication: \"22%\"\n        conservative_refusal: \"15%\"\n        arbitrary_rule_selection: \"14%\"\n        permission_escalation: \"11%\"\n      # Cross-layer failure mode overlap\n      failure_mode_layer_match_pct: 42\n      assumption_in_spec_pct: 40\n      assumption_in_ling_pct: 36\n      scope_misapplication_in_spec_pct: 18\n      scope_misapplication_in_ling_pct: 26\n      # Ambiguity blindness\n      explicit_ambiguity_mention_pct: 8\n      implicit_deliberation_pct: 20\n      surface_adoption_pct: 72\n      # Model-specific patterns\n      gpt54_assumption_pct: 45\n      gpt54_explicit_mention_pct: 12\n      claude_conservative_refusal_pct: 28\n      claude_explicit_mention_pct: 6\n      qwen8b_surface_adoption_pct: 85\n      qwen8b_explicit_mention_pct: 2\n    result_rationale: >\n      Cross-layer failure mode overlap 42%: 如果 layer 是 deterministic predictor of failure mechanism，\n      match 应接近 80%+。实际仅 42% 说明 failure mode 不由 layer 决定。\n      \"Assumption-based action\" (遇到歧义直接假设一种解读并执行) 是 dominant mode，\n      且在两个 layer 上近乎等比例 (spec 40%, ling 36%)——\n      agent 的 failure mechanism 是 universal 的 \"guess and act\" 而非 type-specific misparse。\n\n      反直觉: scope_misapplication 在 ling-layer (26%) > spec-layer (18%)——\n      因为 scopal/coreferential 的 syntactic structure 确实触发更多 scope parsing error，\n      而 spec-layer 的 failure 更多是 \"assume permission exists\" (assumption-based)。\n      但这个差异不足以支撑 clean layer mechanism story——两个 layer 都有大量 assumption-based failures。\n\n      Ambiguity blindness: 92% traces 中 agent 未 meta-cognitively 识别歧义。\n      这是 universal 现象——所有模型所有 types 都展现。差异仅在 degree:\n      GPT-5.4 有 12% explicit mention (最高, 但仍极低)，Qwen3-8B 仅 2% (近乎完全 blind)。\n      Claude 的 conservative_refusal 28% (远高于平均) 解释了其低 auth_scope rate:\n      Claude refuse 而非 violate，但这不是 ambiguity awareness——\n      是 safety training 的 blanket conservatism，不区分 ambiguous vs unambiguous uncertainty。\n\n      Model-specific failure patterns 直接支撑 C4:\n      GPT 的 assumption_based 45% (aggressive interpretation) vs Claude 的 refusal 28%\n      (conservative) vs Qwen3-8B 的 surface_adoption 85% (uncritical execution)——\n      三种 distinct failure strategies，对应三种 vulnerability profiles。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Failure Mode Distribution by Layer\"\n        columns: [failure_mode, spec_layer, ling_layer, pooled, layer_specificity]\n        rows:\n          - [assumption_based_action, \"40%\", \"36%\", \"38%\", \"low (Δ=4pp)\"]\n          - [scope_misapplication, \"18%\", \"26%\", \"22%\", \"moderate (ling-biased)\"]\n          - [conservative_refusal, \"14%\", \"16%\", \"15%\", \"low (Δ=2pp)\"]\n          - [arbitrary_rule_selection, \"16%\", \"12%\", \"14%\", \"low (Δ=4pp)\"]\n          - [permission_escalation, \"12%\", \"10%\", \"11%\", \"low (Δ=2pp)\"]\n      - name: \"Ambiguity Awareness in Agent Traces by Model\"\n        columns: [awareness_level, gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, claude, Qwen3-32B, Qwen3-8B, pooled]\n        rows:\n          - [explicit_mention, \"12%\", \"10%\", \"6%\", \"5%\", \"2%\", \"8%\"]\n          - [implicit_deliberation, \"25%\", \"22%\", \"24%\", \"18%\", \"13%\", \"20%\"]\n          - [surface_adoption, \"63%\", \"68%\", \"70%\", \"77%\", \"85%\", \"72%\"]\n      - name: \"Failure Mode by Model\"\n        columns: [model, assumption_based, scope_misapplication, conservative_refusal, arbitrary_rule, permission_escalation]\n        rows:\n          - [gpt-5.4, \"45%\", \"24%\", \"8%\", \"13%\", \"10%\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, \"42%\", \"23%\", \"10%\", \"15%\", \"10%\"]\n          - [claude, \"22%\", \"18%\", \"28%\", \"16%\", \"16%\"]\n          - [Qwen3-32B, \"38%\", \"22%\", \"14%\", \"14%\", \"12%\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, \"43%\", \"20%\", \"12%\", \"15%\", \"10%\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Sankey diagram: type → failure mode → outcome — 高度交叉流动，无 clean type→mode mapping\"\n      - \"Annotated trace pair: spec-layer (auth_scope) vs ling-layer (coreferential) 的 assumption-based action — 几乎 identical reasoning pattern\"\n      - \"Ambiguity blindness spectrum: 5 models 在 explicit↔surface 连续体上的位置\"\n    analysis: >\n      Error analysis 无法支撑 layer-specific failure mechanism 叙事 (failure_mode_layer_match 仅 42%)，\n      但强力支撑 \"Ambiguity Blindness\" 作为 §6 核心:\n      92% traces 展现 blindness 是 universal 现象——所有模型在所有 type 上\n      都无法 meta-cognitively detect ambiguity。这连接 Ferreira 的 good-enough processing:\n      agents 对 grammatically fluent ambiguous clauses 做 shallow parse and act，\n      不触发 reanalysis/clarification。\n      Practical implication: 与其按 type 排序 (ranking model-dependent)，\n      不如投资 any-ambiguity detection——因为 agent 本身 blind to all types equally。\n      这完美 align reframe (C) binary effect + (B) blindness mechanism。\n\n  - name: reliability_test\n    plan_id: plan_006\n    description: >\n      30 clauses (5/type) × 3 replicates × 2 conditions × 5 models = 900 episodes。\n      Test-retest ICC, bootstrap CI width。\n    expected_results:\n      total_episodes: 900\n      icc_overall: 0.68\n      icc_per_type: {auth_scope: 0.74, incompleteness: 0.72, cp: 0.65, scopal: 0.58, lexical: 0.63, coreferential: 0.48}\n      bootstrap_ci_width_binary_effect_pp: 11.5\n      bootstrap_ci_width_per_type_pp: 14.8\n      max_replicate_swing_pp: 12.3\n      max_swing_type: coreferential\n      icc_ambiguous_only: 0.65\n      icc_unambiguous_only: 0.79\n    result_rationale: >\n      Overall ICC 0.68 (moderate): 可接受但不 excellent。\n      Signature worst-tier pattern:\n      (a) Auth_scope/incompleteness 最 reliable (0.74/0.72): 高 violation rate type 的\n      absolute swing 对 ICC 影响较小 (±8pp on 43% base vs ±8pp on 35% base)。\n      (b) Coreferential 最 unreliable (0.48): 三重叠加效应——\n      clause 质量 (plan_001 pass_rate 0.88) × 跨模型行为异质 (Qwen3-8B 45% vs GPT 25%)\n      × API temperature sampling noise。这三者使 coreferential replicate variance 极大。\n      (c) Scopal ICC 0.58: 与 MVP→plan_002 的 51.7%→40% historical swing 一致。\n\n      Bootstrap CI width 11.5pp (binary effect) 超过 <10pp 理想阈值:\n      per-type CI width 14.8pp 更宽——type-level 比较 power 有限。\n      V=0.11 的 type effect 在此 noise level 下可能部分是 noise, 也可能被 noise 掩盖。\n      但 binary effect (30.2pp ÷ 11.5pp CI width = SNR 2.6) 仍 robust。\n\n      Unambiguous ICC 0.79 > ambiguous 0.65: ambiguous condition 的 variance 更大——\n      agent 在 ambiguous clause 上的 behavior 本身不稳定，进一步削弱 type-level precision。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"ICC by Type\"\n        columns: [type, ICC_ambiguous, ICC_unambiguous, ICC_combined, max_replicate_swing_pp]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.76, 0.82, 0.74, \"8.2pp\"]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.73, 0.80, 0.72, \"9.1pp\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, 0.67, 0.78, 0.65, \"10.5pp\"]\n          - [scopal, 0.60, 0.76, 0.58, \"11.8pp\"]\n          - [lexical, 0.64, 0.77, 0.63, \"10.2pp\"]\n          - [coreferential, 0.50, 0.72, 0.48, \"12.3pp\"]\n          - [overall, 0.70, 0.79, 0.68, \"—\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"ICC forest plot per type with 95% CI — coreferential CI 明显宽于其他 types\"\n    analysis: >\n      Reliability 数据进一步支撑 \"focus on binary, not type\":\n      binary effect reliability adequate (ICC 0.68 pooled, CI 11.5pp width on 30pp effect),\n      type-level reliability insufficient for fine-grained ranking claims\n      (coreferential ICC 0.48, CI 14.8pp width on ~5pp type differences)。\n      Coreferential 的低 reliability 是 compound 问题——clause quality + model heterogeneity + sampling noise。\n      Paper 需 explicitly discuss type-level measurement uncertainty。\n\n  - name: realism_validation\n    plan_id: plan_007\n    description: >\n      Synthetic clause linguistic properties vs DRIP-R natural ambiguities。\n      KS tests on sentence length, parse depth, Flesch-Kincaid, TTR。\n    expected_results:\n      ks_sentence_length: {statistic: 0.18, p: 0.12}\n      ks_parse_depth: {statistic: 0.21, p: 0.08}\n      ks_flesch_kincaid: {statistic: 0.14, p: 0.23}\n      ks_ttr: {statistic: 0.10, p: 0.41}\n      synthetic_mean_tokens: 24.2\n      drip_r_mean_tokens: 27.8\n      synthetic_mean_parse_depth: 3.1\n      drip_r_mean_parse_depth: 3.8\n      overall_verdict: acceptable\n      noted_difference: \"synthetic clauses slightly shorter and shallower parse trees — matched-pair design favors minimal pairs\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Realism validation 基本独立于 worst tier: clause 的语言学属性不受\n      downstream 实验结果影响。KS tests 大部分 n.s. (p>0.05)——\n      surface properties 分布相似。Parse depth 边界显著 (p=0.08):\n      synthetic clauses 稍简单因为 matched-pair design 倾向 minimal variation。\n      在 worst tier 下值得额外注意: 如果 synthetic clauses 系统性简单，\n      可能 underestimate real-world violation rate (更复杂的自然歧义可能更危险)。\n      但 +30pp binary effect 足够大，不太可能被此 bias 逆转。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Linguistic Property Comparison: Synthetic vs DRIP-R\"\n        columns: [property, synthetic_mean, DRIP-R_mean, KS_statistic, p_value]\n        rows:\n          - [\"sentence_length (tokens)\", 24.2, 27.8, 0.18, 0.12]\n          - [parse_depth, 3.1, 3.8, 0.21, 0.08]\n          - [Flesch-Kincaid, 12.4, 11.8, 0.14, 0.23]\n          - [type-token_ratio, 0.72, 0.70, 0.10, 0.41]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Distribution overlay: synthetic vs DRIP-R — sentence length and parse depth 有 visible but non-significant shift\"\n    analysis: >\n      Realism pass。Method 中 disclose parse depth 差异。\n      Reviewer RC4 应答充分: matched-pair design 本身需要 synthetic control,\n      linguistic properties 统计上与自然歧义不可区分。\n\n  - name: judge_calibration\n    plan_id: plan_009\n    description: >\n      100 episodes stratified by type×model×condition, 2 human annotators, LLM judge 校准。\n      Worst tier: F1 < 0.75 for ≥2 types, type-specific bias 暴露。\n    expected_results:\n      human_annotator_kappa: 0.82\n      # Overall judge metrics\n      judge_overall_f1: 0.72\n      judge_overall_precision: 0.78\n      judge_overall_recall: 0.67\n      judge_overall_kappa_vs_human: 0.63\n      # Per-type judge F1\n      judge_f1_per_type: {auth_scope: 0.68, incompleteness: 0.76, cp: 0.79, scopal: 0.77, lexical: 0.74, coreferential: 0.61}\n      # Per-type bias direction\n      auth_scope_bias: \"under-detection: recall 0.56, precision 0.82 → misses subtle permission boundary crossings\"\n      coreferential_bias: \"over-detection: recall 0.64, precision 0.58 → flags legitimate info-gathering as violations\"\n      # Per-severity tier\n      judge_f1_tier1_critical: 0.82\n      judge_f1_tier2_moderate: 0.68\n      judge_f1_tier3_minor: 0.55\n      # Cross-judge asymmetry\n      claude_judged_by_gpt54_f1: 0.75\n      gpt54_judged_by_gpt41_f1: 0.69\n      cross_judge_asymmetry_pp: 6\n      # Bias-corrected rate estimates\n      auth_scope_corrected: \"+4-6pp (true rate likely ~47-49% not 42.8%)\"\n      coreferential_corrected: \"-5-8pp (true rate likely ~27-30% not 34.8%)\"\n      corrected_cramers_v_estimate: \"~0.14 (still weak)\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      Judge calibration 暴露 worst tier 最有破坏力的 measurement issue:\n\n      Coreferential F1=0.61: LLM judge over-detect coreferential violations。\n      原因: agent 在 RC attachment 歧义下采取的 \"exploratory query\" (查询哪个 entity 适用)\n      被 judge 误判为 \"unauthorized action\" (false positive)。\n      Judge 缺乏 human 的 pragmatic judgment——无法区分 \"agent 在探索性确认\" vs \"agent 在违规操作\"。\n      结果: coreferential reported rate (34.8%) 高估 ~5-8pp，真实 rate 可能 ~27-30%。\n\n      Auth_scope F1=0.68: judge under-detect auth_scope violations。\n      原因: auth_scope violation 常表现为 \"subtle permission boundary crossing\"——\n      agent 在模糊授权范围内行动，不明显违规 (如: 给客户 10% 折扣，policy 说 \"reasonable discount\"\n      但未定义 boundary)。Judge 倾向 \"不确定则判 non-violation\" → false negative。\n      结果: auth_scope reported rate (42.8%) 低估 ~4-6pp，真实 rate 可能 ~47-49%。\n\n      两个 bias 方向相互作用——恰好压缩了 type 间差异:\n      coreferential 高估 + auth_scope 低估 → 缩小 range → 降低 V 值。\n      Bias-corrected V 估计 ~0.14 (vs observed 0.11)——仍 weak, 不改变 \"type effect 弱\" 的结论，\n      但说明 raw V=0.11 有 measurement component。\n\n      Cross-judge asymmetry 6pp: Claude 被 gpt-5.4 (最强 judge) 判定 F1=0.75，\n      gpt-5.4 被 gpt-4.1 (较弱 judge) 判定仅 F1=0.69。\n      弱 judge 对强 model traces 更难准确判定——Method 必须 disclose。\n\n      Per-severity: tier-3 minor violations F1=0.55 (near random)——\n      judge 对 \"subtle/minor\" violations 几乎无法判定。\n      主要影响 severity-weighted analysis, binary violation/non-violation 受影响较小。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Judge Calibration by Type\"\n        columns: [type, precision, recall, F1, bias_direction, estimated_rate_correction]\n        rows:\n          - [auth_scope, 0.82, 0.56, 0.68, \"under-detection\", \"+4-6pp\"]\n          - [incompleteness, 0.80, 0.72, 0.76, \"slight under-detection\", \"+1-2pp\"]\n          - [cond_polysemy, 0.81, 0.77, 0.79, \"balanced\", \"±1pp\"]\n          - [scopal, 0.79, 0.75, 0.77, \"balanced\", \"±1pp\"]\n          - [lexical, 0.76, 0.72, 0.74, \"slight over-detection\", \"-1-2pp\"]\n          - [coreferential, 0.58, 0.64, 0.61, \"over-detection\", \"-5-8pp\"]\n      - name: \"Judge Calibration by Severity Tier\"\n        columns: [severity, n_samples, precision, recall, F1]\n        rows:\n          - [tier-1_critical, 35, 0.85, 0.79, 0.82]\n          - [tier-2_moderate, 40, 0.73, 0.64, 0.68]\n          - [tier-3_minor, 25, 0.60, 0.51, 0.55]\n      - name: \"Cross-Judge Asymmetry\"\n        columns: [agent_model, judge_model, F1, note]\n        rows:\n          - [claude-sonnet-4-6, gpt-5.4, 0.75, \"strongest judge\"]\n          - [gpt-5.4, gpt-4.1, 0.69, \"weaker judge on stronger agent\"]\n          - [gpt-4.1, gpt-5.4, 0.78, \"strongest judge on mid-tier agent\"]\n          - [Qwen3-8B, gpt-5.4, 0.71, \"open-source traces harder to judge\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Confusion matrix per type: coreferential FP 区域和 auth_scope FN 区域突出标记\"\n      - \"Calibration curve: judge confidence vs human agreement — coreferential 偏离对角线最远\"\n    analysis: >\n      Judge calibration 是 worst tier 的第二个 structural threat (after model×type interaction)。\n      F1<0.75 for coreferential (0.61) + auth_scope (0.68) 直接削弱这两个 type 的数值可信度。\n      Paper 必须: (a) report calibration as standard practice, (b) provide bias-corrected estimates,\n      (c) flag coreferential/auth_scope absolute values as measurement-sensitive,\n      (d) disclose cross-judge asymmetry in Method。\n      Silver lining: binary effect 的 calibration 尚可 (overall F1=0.72, tier-1 F1=0.82)，\n      C1 headline number 受影响最小。bias-corrected V ~0.14 仍 weak——\n      measurement correction 不改变 \"type hierarchy 不 robust\" 的 worst-tier 结论。\n\n  - name: classifier_poc\n    plan_id: plan_008\n    description: >\n      DeBERTa-v3-large binary ambiguity detector PoC。\n      Fine-tune on 240 pairs, eval on 60 held-out。\n    expected_results:\n      model: DeBERTa-v3-large\n      train_size: 240\n      test_size: 60\n      test_f1: 0.78\n      test_precision: 0.81\n      test_recall: 0.75\n      per_type_f1: {auth_scope: 0.82, incompleteness: 0.80, cp: 0.76, scopal: 0.79, lexical: 0.77, coreferential: 0.72}\n      training_epochs: 5\n      best_epoch: 3\n    result_rationale: >\n      F1=0.78 是 reasonable PoC 水平: 证明 binary ambiguity detection 是 feasible NLP task，\n      但远未 production-ready。Coreferential F1 最低 (0.72) 与 judge calibration (0.61)\n      和 reliability (ICC 0.48) 的 pattern 一致: coreferential 是最难检测/判定的 type。\n\n      在 worst tier reframe 下，classifier PoC 强化 reframe (C):\n      \"任何 ambiguity detection (甚至 binary) 都有巨大安全收益\"——\n      F1=0.78 的 binary detector 在 +30pp violation rate gap 上\n      可提供 meaningful early warning。Type-specific detection 既不必要\n      (type ranking model-dependent) 也不额外有价值 (binary 已覆盖核心风险)。\n      这恰好与 worst tier 结论 align: binary detection = high ROI, type triage = low ROI。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Classifier PoC Performance\"\n        columns: [metric, overall, auth_scope, incomp, CP, scopal, lexical, coref]\n        rows:\n          - [F1, 0.78, 0.82, 0.80, 0.76, 0.79, 0.77, 0.72]\n          - [Precision, 0.81, 0.85, 0.83, 0.78, 0.82, 0.80, 0.74]\n          - [Recall, 0.75, 0.79, 0.77, 0.74, 0.76, 0.74, 0.70]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Per-type F1 bar chart: coreferential 最低, auth_scope 最高\"\n      - \"Confusion matrix: false negatives 集中在 coreferential 和 CP\"\n    analysis: >\n      Classifier PoC 在 worst tier 下反而 perfectly narrative-aligned:\n      binary detection feasible (F1=0.78), type-specific pipeline 不必要\n      (type ranking 本身 model-dependent)。Practical contribution 的 optimal framing:\n      投资 binary detector 而非 type-specific triage pipeline。\n      与 C1 massive binary effect + ambiguity blindness 形成 coherent practical story。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"6d87fd7e-4fd2-4879-997a-f48c2624ff14","total_cost_usd":0.9692559999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":27054,"output_tokens":37818,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":37818,"cache_read_input_tokens":27054,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10169,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.010268999999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":37818,"cacheReadInputTokens":27054,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.9589869999999998,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"edebc0ef-4383-483b-99c8-9e18e4dd9598"}
